1
00:01:06,780 --> 00:01:08,498
[Metallic clanking]

2
00:01:18,980 --> 00:01:21,778
[Dramatic instrumental music, background]

3
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:48,739
Can I persuade you to take a sandwich?

4
00:01:49,220 --> 00:01:50,812
I'll get drive-through.

5
00:01:51,900 --> 00:01:53,538
[Batmobile engine roars]

6
00:02:04,900 --> 00:02:06,777
[Engine revs in acceleration]

7
00:02:11,660 --> 00:02:13,696
<i>[Batman Forever theme song plays]</i>

8
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:19,092
[Crowd shouting]

9
00:02:24,580 --> 00:02:26,252
[High-pitched screeching]

10
00:02:30,460 --> 00:02:33,770
You're counting on the Winged Avenger
to deliver you from evil...

11
00:02:33,860 --> 00:02:35,532
...aren't you, my friend?

12
00:02:35,620 --> 00:02:36,814
[Chuckles softly]

13
00:02:36,900 --> 00:02:38,618
Are you going to kill me?

14
00:02:38,900 --> 00:02:42,210
Maybe, maybe not.
We're of two minds on the subject.

15
00:02:44,660 --> 00:02:46,730
TWO-FACE: Are you a gambling man?

16
00:02:47,380 --> 00:02:49,211
Let's say we flip for it?

17
00:02:50,260 --> 00:02:53,297
TWO-FACE: One man is born a hero,
his brother a coward.

18
00:02:53,460 --> 00:02:56,213
[Whispers] Babies starve,
politicians grow fat...

19
00:02:56,980 --> 00:03:00,177
...holy men are martyred,
and junkies grow legion.

20
00:03:00,980 --> 00:03:02,049
Why?

21
00:03:02,740 --> 00:03:04,810
TWO-FACE: Why, why, why, why, why?

22
00:03:05,820 --> 00:03:06,935
Luck!

23
00:03:07,460 --> 00:03:09,928
[Shouts] Blind, stupid, simple, doo-dah...

24
00:03:11,140 --> 00:03:12,778
...clueless luck!

25
00:03:12,860 --> 00:03:13,929
[Cackles]

26
00:03:15,940 --> 00:03:17,771
TWO-FACE: The random toss...

27
00:03:18,740 --> 00:03:20,571
...is the only true justice.

28
00:03:20,660 --> 00:03:23,299
Let's see what justice has in store...

29
00:03:24,500 --> 00:03:25,694
...for you.

30
00:03:28,420 --> 00:03:29,739
[Chuckles]

31
00:03:30,740 --> 00:03:32,776
TWO-FACE: [Whispers]
It's like the touch of God.

32
00:03:32,860 --> 00:03:34,498
Wait, wait, wait.

33
00:03:35,540 --> 00:03:36,529
[Gasps]

34
00:03:37,460 --> 00:03:39,769
Fortune smiles.
Another day of wine and roses.

35
00:03:39,860 --> 00:03:41,737
In your case, beer and pizza.

36
00:03:42,220 --> 00:03:43,812
TWO-FACE: Out of here, guys!

37
00:03:43,900 --> 00:03:46,972
BANK GUARD: You said you'd let me live!
TWO-FACE: Too true!

38
00:03:47,060 --> 00:03:50,575
TWO-FACE: And so you shall! Nothing's
better than live bait to trap a bat.

39
00:03:50,660 --> 00:03:52,571
[Chaotic reactions from crowd]

40
00:03:55,980 --> 00:03:58,289
<i>[Batman Forever theme song plays,
background]</i>

41
00:03:58,380 --> 00:04:00,655
[Crowd shouting and talking excitedly]

42
00:04:05,300 --> 00:04:06,653
Hot entrance.

43
00:04:07,380 --> 00:04:08,335
Two-Face?

44
00:04:08,420 --> 00:04:09,535
Two guards are dead.

45
00:04:09,620 --> 00:04:11,929
He's holding a third hostage.
Didn't see this one coming.

46
00:04:12,020 --> 00:04:13,453
CHASE: We should have.

47
00:04:13,540 --> 00:04:15,132
The Second Bank of Gotham...

48
00:04:15,220 --> 00:04:17,370
BATMAN: Second anniversary
of the day I captured him.

49
00:04:17,460 --> 00:04:18,893
CHASE: How could he resist?

50
00:04:18,980 --> 00:04:20,333
I'm Chase Meridian.

51
00:04:20,420 --> 00:04:24,811
COMMISSIONER: I asked her to come here
to consult on the case. She specializes in...

52
00:04:24,900 --> 00:04:28,097
Abnormal psychology,
multiple personalities. I read your work.

53
00:04:28,180 --> 00:04:29,249
Insightful.

54
00:04:29,340 --> 00:04:30,898
Naive, but insightful.

55
00:04:31,060 --> 00:04:34,655
I'm flattered. Not every girl
makes a superhero's night table.

56
00:04:34,820 --> 00:04:36,173
COMMISSIONER: Can we reason with him?

57
00:04:36,260 --> 00:04:37,613
He's got innocent people up there.

58
00:04:37,700 --> 00:04:39,053
CHASE: It won't do any good.

59
00:04:39,140 --> 00:04:40,573
He'll slaughter them without a thought.

60
00:04:40,660 --> 00:04:41,695
BATMAN: Agreed.

61
00:04:41,780 --> 00:04:45,250
A trauma powerful enough to create
an alternate personality leaves one...

62
00:04:45,340 --> 00:04:48,377
CHASE: In a world where normal rules
of right and wrong no longer apply.

63
00:04:48,460 --> 00:04:49,210
Exactly.

64
00:04:49,300 --> 00:04:50,619
CHASE: Like you.

65
00:04:51,300 --> 00:04:55,452
I could write a hell of a paper on a man
who dresses like a flying rodent.

66
00:04:56,980 --> 00:04:59,096
Bats aren't rodents, Dr. Meridian.

67
00:04:59,700 --> 00:05:01,770
Really? I didn't know that.

68
00:05:02,340 --> 00:05:03,819
You are interesting.

69
00:05:03,900 --> 00:05:05,777
[Propellers pelting overhead]

70
00:05:06,180 --> 00:05:07,852
And call me Chase.

71
00:05:10,020 --> 00:05:13,296
By the way, do you have a first name,
or do I call you Bats?

72
00:05:13,380 --> 00:05:15,610
[Chaotic reactions from crowd]

73
00:05:17,060 --> 00:05:19,051
[Dramatic instrumental beat, background]

74
00:05:19,140 --> 00:05:21,210
Let's start this party with a bang!

75
00:05:21,300 --> 00:05:22,813
[Thunderous crashing]

76
00:05:25,380 --> 00:05:26,449
[Cackles]

77
00:05:27,300 --> 00:05:28,449
[Bell rings]

78
00:05:30,180 --> 00:05:32,740
Very punctual, even for his own funeral.
Boys!

79
00:05:33,340 --> 00:05:34,978
TWO-FACE: Kill the Bat!

80
00:05:37,300 --> 00:05:38,494
[Cackles]

81
00:05:39,260 --> 00:05:40,534
[Cackles]

82
00:05:44,660 --> 00:05:45,775
[Bell rings]

83
00:05:45,860 --> 00:05:47,009
Blast him!

84
00:05:47,100 --> 00:05:48,818
[Rapid machine-gun blasts]

85
00:05:56,460 --> 00:05:57,449
[Silence]

86
00:05:59,300 --> 00:06:00,699
Open sesame.

87
00:06:00,780 --> 00:06:02,213
[Metallic scraping]

88
00:06:08,180 --> 00:06:09,579
[Two-Face grunts]

89
00:06:10,540 --> 00:06:12,451
[Grunting and groaning]

90
00:06:16,540 --> 00:06:19,373
[Fast-paced instrumental music,
background]

91
00:06:22,700 --> 00:06:23,689
[Zap]

92
00:06:29,580 --> 00:06:30,899
[Groaning]

93
00:06:31,380 --> 00:06:32,369
[Wailing]

94
00:06:40,860 --> 00:06:42,771
[Grunting and groaning]

95
00:06:44,460 --> 00:06:46,257
[Huffing and puffing]

96
00:06:48,140 --> 00:06:49,414
[Yelling]

97
00:06:57,660 --> 00:06:59,059
[Muffled shouting]

98
00:07:01,900 --> 00:07:02,889
Ouch!

99
00:07:03,060 --> 00:07:04,698
BANK GUARD: It's a trap!

100
00:07:06,620 --> 00:07:08,178
[Short, rapid gasps]

101
00:07:09,180 --> 00:07:11,455
[Loud, distorted sound effects]

102
00:07:16,180 --> 00:07:17,169
Oh, no!

103
00:07:18,780 --> 00:07:21,374
[More distorted and echoing sound effects]

104
00:07:22,340 --> 00:07:23,819
[Bank guard screams]

105
00:07:29,020 --> 00:07:31,488
[Chaotic yelling and screaming from crowd]

106
00:07:35,100 --> 00:07:37,170
[Instrumental music continues,
background]

107
00:07:37,260 --> 00:07:40,491
<i>TWO-FACE ON LOUDSPEAKER:
Attention citizens of fair Gotham!</i>

108
00:07:41,060 --> 00:07:42,573
[Cackles hysterically]

109
00:07:42,860 --> 00:07:46,296
<i>When we open that safe,
we'll have everything we ever wanted:</i>

110
00:07:46,460 --> 00:07:50,692
<i>Enough cash to rain down upon
fair Gotham, a glorious flood of chaos.</i>

111
00:07:51,100 --> 00:07:52,738
<i>And, of course...</i>

112
00:07:53,020 --> 00:07:54,533
<i>... you, my boy, dead!</i>

113
00:07:54,620 --> 00:07:56,053
[Two-Face chuckles]

114
00:07:56,740 --> 00:07:57,729
Oh, no!

115
00:07:58,300 --> 00:08:00,211
BANK GUARD: It's boiling acid!

116
00:08:01,180 --> 00:08:05,856
<i>For your dying pleasure, we are serving
the acid that made us the men we are!</i>

117
00:08:05,940 --> 00:08:07,612
BANK GUARD: [Shrieks] No!

118
00:08:09,580 --> 00:08:11,571
BATMAN: Hold on.
BANK GUARD: Yes!

119
00:08:12,180 --> 00:08:13,613
[Cackles hysterically]

120
00:08:13,700 --> 00:08:15,179
TWO-FACE: Haul away!

121
00:08:15,420 --> 00:08:17,012
Yes! Haul away!

122
00:08:17,700 --> 00:08:19,213
[Mechanical rattling]

123
00:08:22,300 --> 00:08:25,098
BATMAN: Give me your hand.
BANK GUARD: [Cries] Don't let go!

124
00:08:25,180 --> 00:08:26,169
Aah!

125
00:08:28,060 --> 00:08:29,049
[Wailing]

126
00:08:29,980 --> 00:08:31,732
BATMAN: Need to borrow this.

127
00:08:32,820 --> 00:08:34,014
[Shrieks] Hey!

128
00:08:34,940 --> 00:08:36,817
BANK GUARD: That's my hearing aid!

129
00:08:36,900 --> 00:08:38,015
Thanks.

130
00:08:41,980 --> 00:08:44,210
BANK GUARD: Wow!
My shoes are melting!

131
00:08:50,140 --> 00:08:52,938
[Dramatic instrumental music, background]

132
00:08:53,820 --> 00:08:55,253
BANK GUARD: [Shrieks] No more!

133
00:08:55,340 --> 00:08:56,739
[Two-Face screams]

134
00:09:00,460 --> 00:09:01,449
[Hissing]

135
00:09:02,580 --> 00:09:03,649
[Clank]

136
00:09:06,980 --> 00:09:08,652
[Bank guard gasps]

137
00:09:10,180 --> 00:09:11,135
Hang on.

138
00:09:11,300 --> 00:09:12,619
[Gasps] Hang on?

139
00:09:13,500 --> 00:09:14,774
[Hissing]

140
00:09:16,660 --> 00:09:18,218
[Bank guard screaming]

141
00:09:24,620 --> 00:09:26,338
[Loud, distorted rumbling]

142
00:09:31,380 --> 00:09:32,449
[Coughs]

143
00:09:33,380 --> 00:09:34,733
COMMISSIONER: Get him down.

144
00:09:34,820 --> 00:09:36,014
Get him down.

145
00:09:37,220 --> 00:09:39,051
Take it easy with him.

146
00:09:39,140 --> 00:09:41,938
COMMISSIONER: You'll be all right.
Just stay calm.

147
00:09:48,580 --> 00:09:49,854
[Zooming]

148
00:09:53,060 --> 00:09:54,778
[Cackles] This'll fix him!

149
00:10:01,060 --> 00:10:02,288
TWO-FACE: Hang on, Batty!

150
00:10:02,380 --> 00:10:03,893
[Cackles hysterically]

151
00:10:10,460 --> 00:10:11,734
[Cackles]

152
00:10:13,780 --> 00:10:15,213
[Roaring explosion]

153
00:10:22,500 --> 00:10:23,899
[Gasps] Let's see.

154
00:10:24,220 --> 00:10:25,414
TWO-FACE: Yes!

155
00:10:25,660 --> 00:10:28,538
Yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes!
Oh, happy day!

156
00:10:28,620 --> 00:10:29,689
[Cackles]

157
00:10:30,700 --> 00:10:32,338
Farewell forever to that...

158
00:10:32,420 --> 00:10:34,456
...pointy-eared night rat!

159
00:10:36,900 --> 00:10:38,015
PILOT: Face!

160
00:10:40,180 --> 00:10:41,499
Hey, Face!

161
00:10:43,220 --> 00:10:44,255
[Cackles]

162
00:10:44,340 --> 00:10:45,534
[Screams] No!

163
00:10:45,660 --> 00:10:47,696
[Rapid machine-gun blasts]

164
00:10:58,340 --> 00:11:00,137
[Bang, Two-Face grunts]

165
00:11:00,220 --> 00:11:01,289
[Smash]

166
00:11:01,500 --> 00:11:03,411
You need help. Give it up.

167
00:11:06,580 --> 00:11:08,059
[Short, rapid gasps]

168
00:11:12,020 --> 00:11:14,818
[Dramatic instrumental music, background]

169
00:11:20,660 --> 00:11:21,729
[Cackles]

170
00:11:25,540 --> 00:11:27,610
Have the good taste to die!

171
00:11:29,060 --> 00:11:30,288
See you!

172
00:11:32,860 --> 00:11:34,657
[Cackles hysterically]

173
00:11:41,580 --> 00:11:43,411
[Thunderous explosion]

174
00:11:56,540 --> 00:11:58,815
<i>[Batman Forever theme song, background]</i>

175
00:12:03,500 --> 00:12:04,694
[Gasps]

176
00:12:09,340 --> 00:12:12,173
<i>NEWSCASTER: Despite a valiant effort
last night by Batman...</i>

177
00:12:12,260 --> 00:12:15,855
<i>... Harvey Two-Face is still at large
and extremely dangerous.</i>

178
00:12:16,100 --> 00:12:17,294
<i>In other news today...</i>

179
00:12:17,380 --> 00:12:20,497
<i>... billionaire Bruce Wayne extended
his profit-sharing program...</i>

180
00:12:20,580 --> 00:12:25,290
<i>... to the employees of the successful
electronics branch of Wayne Enterprises.</i>

181
00:12:25,780 --> 00:12:27,577
[Elevator bell rings]

182
00:12:29,660 --> 00:12:31,651
[Upbeat instrumental music, background]

183
00:12:31,740 --> 00:12:32,889
[Hiss]

184
00:12:35,620 --> 00:12:37,099
STICKLEY: Mr. Wayne.

185
00:12:38,500 --> 00:12:41,572
STICKLEY: Your inspections are
a departmental highlight.

186
00:12:41,700 --> 00:12:43,577
[Gasps] Oh, my God, it's him.

187
00:12:45,020 --> 00:12:46,931
I am a winner. I am a winner.

188
00:12:47,100 --> 00:12:48,499
I am a winner.

189
00:12:48,940 --> 00:12:50,134
I am a winner.

190
00:12:50,220 --> 00:12:51,858
[Riddler doll chuckles]

191
00:12:52,380 --> 00:12:54,814
Bioremediation. Alternative fuel.

192
00:12:55,260 --> 00:12:56,978
Mr. Wayne, look at that time.

193
00:12:57,060 --> 00:13:00,336
Perhaps we should get to R & D
as soon as possible.

194
00:13:01,540 --> 00:13:02,768
Mister...?

195
00:13:03,620 --> 00:13:05,212
Oh, Bruce Wayne.

196
00:13:06,340 --> 00:13:08,729
No, that's my name. And you are?

197
00:13:09,340 --> 00:13:10,375
[Gasps] Nygma.

198
00:13:10,460 --> 00:13:11,415
Edward.

199
00:13:11,540 --> 00:13:13,974
Edward Nygma. You hired me personally.

200
00:13:14,300 --> 00:13:16,336
EDWARD: Just like I tell everyone.

201
00:13:16,580 --> 00:13:21,131
We've never actually met, but your name
was on the hiring slip. I have it.

202
00:13:22,340 --> 00:13:23,853
I need that hand back.

203
00:13:24,740 --> 00:13:26,458
Oh, yes, of course.

204
00:13:26,740 --> 00:13:28,059
I'm sorry.

205
00:13:28,340 --> 00:13:29,819
It's just that...

206
00:13:30,980 --> 00:13:32,572
[Whispers]... you're my idol.

207
00:13:32,660 --> 00:13:33,570
Back to work.

208
00:13:33,660 --> 00:13:36,493
And some people have been trying
to keep us apart.

209
00:13:37,220 --> 00:13:38,653
Back to work.

210
00:13:38,900 --> 00:13:40,174
BRUCE: It's okay.

211
00:13:40,260 --> 00:13:42,012
What's on your mind?

212
00:13:42,180 --> 00:13:43,454
Precisely.

213
00:13:43,700 --> 00:13:45,452
What's on all our minds?

214
00:13:46,020 --> 00:13:47,373
Brain waves.

215
00:13:47,460 --> 00:13:48,449
[Giggles]

216
00:13:51,620 --> 00:13:53,133
EDWARD: The future...

217
00:13:53,260 --> 00:13:55,216
...of Wayne Enterprises...

218
00:13:56,180 --> 00:13:57,818
...is brain waves.

219
00:13:59,380 --> 00:14:01,291
STICKLEY: I must apologize, Mr. Wayne.

220
00:14:01,380 --> 00:14:04,258
- I terminated his project today.
- It's okay.

221
00:14:04,580 --> 00:14:05,615
EDWARD: I have it!

222
00:14:05,700 --> 00:14:06,769
[Rattling]

223
00:14:08,580 --> 00:14:09,569
<i>Voilä!</i>

224
00:14:13,060 --> 00:14:14,413
[Gasps excitedly]

225
00:14:14,820 --> 00:14:16,333
My invention...

226
00:14:16,500 --> 00:14:19,856
...beams any TV signal directly
into the human brain.

227
00:14:20,660 --> 00:14:23,857
By stimulating neurons,
manipulating brain waves...

228
00:14:24,420 --> 00:14:28,572
EDWARD: this device makes the audience
feel like they're inside the show.

229
00:14:30,020 --> 00:14:32,488
Why be brutalized by an uncaring world?

230
00:14:32,660 --> 00:14:35,333
Did you say "manipulating brain waves"?

231
00:14:36,420 --> 00:14:37,614
[Pants]

232
00:14:38,580 --> 00:14:39,615
Yes.

233
00:14:40,420 --> 00:14:41,569
EDWARD: But...

234
00:14:41,940 --> 00:14:44,693
<i>... someone like you would never need it.</i>

235
00:14:45,380 --> 00:14:46,813
Someone so...

236
00:14:47,380 --> 00:14:49,211
<i>... intelligent, witty and...</i>

237
00:14:49,300 --> 00:14:50,369
[Sirens blaring in distance]

238
00:14:50,460 --> 00:14:51,688
<i>... charming.</i>

239
00:14:52,100 --> 00:14:56,616
I need a bit of additional funding
for human trials. Let me show you, please!

240
00:14:56,740 --> 00:14:57,855
BRUCE: Now, listen...

241
00:14:57,940 --> 00:15:00,898
...I want a full set of technical schematics
on this, okay?

242
00:15:00,980 --> 00:15:03,369
We'll be full partners in this, Bruce.

243
00:15:03,540 --> 00:15:05,610
Look at us! Two of a kind!

244
00:15:06,420 --> 00:15:09,173
You call my assistant, Margaret.
She'll set something up.

245
00:15:09,260 --> 00:15:10,249
Uh...

246
00:15:10,580 --> 00:15:11,695
That's not...

247
00:15:11,780 --> 00:15:13,850
...going to be good for me.

248
00:15:14,580 --> 00:15:16,457
EDWARD: I need an answer now.

249
00:15:17,220 --> 00:15:19,131
[Softly] I think I deserve it.

250
00:15:19,460 --> 00:15:21,849
BRUCE: I'm sorry, then the answer is no.

251
00:15:22,900 --> 00:15:25,050
Tampering with people's brain waves...

252
00:15:25,140 --> 00:15:26,732
...mind manipulation...

253
00:15:27,460 --> 00:15:29,928
...it just raises too many questions.

254
00:15:30,420 --> 00:15:31,535
Sorry.

255
00:15:31,940 --> 00:15:34,932
BRUCE: Thanks, keep up the good work.
The factory looks great.

256
00:15:35,020 --> 00:15:36,339
STICKLEY: All right, everyone!

257
00:15:36,420 --> 00:15:37,694
Back to work!

258
00:15:37,900 --> 00:15:39,811
We'll discuss this later!

259
00:15:44,100 --> 00:15:46,409
[Sobs] You were supposed to understand.

260
00:15:50,580 --> 00:15:52,571
I'll make you understand.

261
00:15:55,300 --> 00:15:57,211
[Dramatic instrumental music, background]

262
00:15:57,300 --> 00:15:58,415
Lock.

263
00:16:04,620 --> 00:16:05,814
BRUCE: Chair.

264
00:16:09,780 --> 00:16:10,769
[Zooming]

265
00:16:13,980 --> 00:16:14,935
Alfred.

266
00:16:15,180 --> 00:16:16,533
<i>ALFRED: I saw the signal.</i>

267
00:16:16,620 --> 00:16:17,814
<i>All is ready.</i>

268
00:16:25,420 --> 00:16:26,535
[Crackling]

269
00:16:29,500 --> 00:16:32,014
<i>[Batman Forever theme song plays,
background]</i>

270
00:16:34,580 --> 00:16:36,218
[Batmobile engine roars]

271
00:16:56,860 --> 00:16:57,929
Commissioner?

272
00:16:58,020 --> 00:16:59,499
CHASE: He's at home.

273
00:17:00,740 --> 00:17:02,412
I sent the signal.

274
00:17:03,540 --> 00:17:04,734
What's wrong?

275
00:17:07,460 --> 00:17:10,657
Last night at the bank I noticed
something about Two-Face:

276
00:17:10,740 --> 00:17:12,059
CHASE: His coin.

277
00:17:12,340 --> 00:17:13,932
It's his Achilles' heel.

278
00:17:14,100 --> 00:17:15,533
It can be exploited.

279
00:17:15,700 --> 00:17:16,928
BATMAN: I know.

280
00:17:17,220 --> 00:17:18,812
You called me for this?

281
00:17:18,900 --> 00:17:20,811
The Batsignal is not a beeper.

282
00:17:21,460 --> 00:17:24,258
I wish I could say that my interest
in you was...

283
00:17:24,460 --> 00:17:26,098
...purely professional.

284
00:17:26,260 --> 00:17:28,012
Are you trying to get under my cape?

285
00:17:28,100 --> 00:17:29,169
[Chase snickers]

286
00:17:29,260 --> 00:17:31,569
A girl can't live by psychoses alone.

287
00:17:31,660 --> 00:17:34,049
It's the car, right? Chicks love it.

288
00:17:34,140 --> 00:17:35,129
[Giggles]

289
00:17:35,460 --> 00:17:37,769
What is it about the wrong kind of man?

290
00:17:38,340 --> 00:17:40,570
In grade school: guys with earrings.

291
00:17:40,780 --> 00:17:43,374
College: motorcycles, leather jackets.

292
00:17:44,340 --> 00:17:45,455
Now...

293
00:17:46,180 --> 00:17:47,374
[Chase moans]

294
00:17:48,860 --> 00:17:50,452
...black rubber.

295
00:17:51,220 --> 00:17:53,370
Try a fireman. Less to take off.

296
00:17:55,740 --> 00:17:59,016
I don't mind the work.
Pity I can't see behind the mask.

297
00:17:59,460 --> 00:18:00,893
BATMAN: We all wear masks.

298
00:18:00,980 --> 00:18:03,414
My life's an open book. You read?

299
00:18:04,300 --> 00:18:06,814
I don't blend in at a family picnic.

300
00:18:07,780 --> 00:18:10,772
CHASE: We could give it a try. I'll bring
the wine...

301
00:18:11,940 --> 00:18:14,010
...you bring your scarred psyche.

302
00:18:16,300 --> 00:18:17,653
Direct, aren't you?

303
00:18:17,740 --> 00:18:19,093
CHASE: You like strong women.

304
00:18:19,180 --> 00:18:20,898
I've done my homework.

305
00:18:21,100 --> 00:18:23,853
Or do I need skintight vinyl and a whip?

306
00:18:24,980 --> 00:18:27,210
I haven't had much luck with women.

307
00:18:27,540 --> 00:18:30,213
Maybe you just haven't met
the right woman.

308
00:18:32,580 --> 00:18:33,729
[Door opens]

309
00:18:34,500 --> 00:18:35,615
[Footsteps]

310
00:18:36,340 --> 00:18:37,329
I saw the signal.

311
00:18:37,420 --> 00:18:40,059
COMMISSIONER: What's going on?
BATMAN: Nothing.

312
00:18:40,420 --> 00:18:41,535
False alarm.

313
00:18:42,260 --> 00:18:43,659
Are you sure?

314
00:18:48,340 --> 00:18:50,774
[Dramatic instrumental music, background]

315
00:19:01,860 --> 00:19:03,009
Women.

316
00:19:03,460 --> 00:19:05,098
[Batmobile engine roars]

317
00:19:06,260 --> 00:19:07,454
[Crackling]

318
00:19:08,620 --> 00:19:10,258
[Edward gasps excitedly]

319
00:19:12,500 --> 00:19:14,092
EDWARD: Now I've got it!

320
00:19:14,380 --> 00:19:15,369
Ha!

321
00:19:17,260 --> 00:19:19,933
"Too many questions.
There's too many questions.

322
00:19:20,100 --> 00:19:21,499
[Whiny voice] "Too many..."

323
00:19:21,580 --> 00:19:22,649
[Sarcastic tittering]

324
00:19:22,740 --> 00:19:24,412
I'll show you it works!

325
00:19:24,580 --> 00:19:27,140
STICKLEY: [Yells]
What the hell is going on here?

326
00:19:27,220 --> 00:19:30,974
I told you this project is terminated!
I'm calling Security!

327
00:19:34,820 --> 00:19:35,809
[Thud]

328
00:19:36,980 --> 00:19:38,971
[Shouts] Caffeine will kill you!

329
00:19:41,780 --> 00:19:42,929
[Ding]

330
00:19:43,260 --> 00:19:45,694
EDWARD: [Whispers]
Rise and shine, little guinea pig.

331
00:19:45,780 --> 00:19:47,213
What are you doing?

332
00:19:47,380 --> 00:19:48,415
Untie me!

333
00:19:48,580 --> 00:19:50,172
EDWARD: This won't hurt.

334
00:19:50,260 --> 00:19:52,251
At least, I don't think it will.

335
00:19:53,420 --> 00:19:55,297
STICKLEY: What are you doing?

336
00:19:56,020 --> 00:19:57,692
You touch that switch and...

337
00:19:57,780 --> 00:19:58,690
This?

338
00:19:59,060 --> 00:20:00,618
[High-pitched zoom]

339
00:20:03,180 --> 00:20:04,374
[Sighs]

340
00:20:05,380 --> 00:20:06,938
[Edward laughs softly]

341
00:20:11,620 --> 00:20:13,338
[Electronic sound effects]

342
00:20:13,860 --> 00:20:15,578
EDWARD: Losing resolution.

343
00:20:15,780 --> 00:20:16,974
More power!

344
00:20:17,060 --> 00:20:18,049
[Zap]

345
00:20:18,140 --> 00:20:19,812
[Stickley screams]

346
00:20:19,940 --> 00:20:21,259
[Both scream]

347
00:20:23,140 --> 00:20:24,732
[Voice vibrates]

348
00:20:25,260 --> 00:20:26,898
[Hoots and hollers]

349
00:20:27,380 --> 00:20:29,769
[Both speak gibberish extremely quickly]

350
00:20:37,060 --> 00:20:38,857
[Sighs exaggeratedly]

351
00:20:39,780 --> 00:20:41,099
[Shouts] Edward Nygma...

352
00:20:41,180 --> 00:20:42,295
...come on down!

353
00:20:42,380 --> 00:20:44,371
You're the next contestant on...

354
00:20:44,460 --> 00:20:45,973
<i>...Brain Drain!</i>

355
00:20:46,060 --> 00:20:48,255
[Imitates voices of talk-show host
and contestant]

356
00:20:48,340 --> 00:20:51,332
I'll take what's inside
thick skull number one!

357
00:20:51,540 --> 00:20:53,258
EDWARD: What have we got for him?

358
00:20:53,340 --> 00:20:54,329
[Goofy chuckling]

359
00:20:54,420 --> 00:20:57,173
Oh, Stickley, I'm having a breakthrough!

360
00:20:57,780 --> 00:20:59,372
And a breakdown? Maybe!

361
00:20:59,620 --> 00:21:02,293
Nevertheless, I'm smarter. I'm a genius.

362
00:21:02,580 --> 00:21:04,377
No, several geniuses.

363
00:21:04,740 --> 00:21:06,492
A gaggle, a swarm...

364
00:21:06,900 --> 00:21:09,130
...a flock of freaking Freuds!

365
00:21:10,500 --> 00:21:12,297
Riddle me this, Fred.

366
00:21:13,140 --> 00:21:14,892
EDWARD: What is everything to someone...

367
00:21:14,980 --> 00:21:17,050
<i>... and nothing to everyone else?</i>

368
00:21:17,540 --> 00:21:19,212
[Shouts] Your mind, baby!

369
00:21:19,380 --> 00:21:22,053
Now mine pumps with the power of yours!

370
00:21:22,500 --> 00:21:24,730
[Sings]
"I'm sucking up your IQ

371
00:21:25,820 --> 00:21:27,412
"Vacuuming your cortex

372
00:21:27,580 --> 00:21:29,298
"Feeding off your brain"

373
00:21:29,380 --> 00:21:31,211
[Electronic musical rhythm]

374
00:21:33,860 --> 00:21:35,088
[Shrieks] Fred!

375
00:21:35,220 --> 00:21:36,539
[Zapping sounds]

376
00:21:43,460 --> 00:21:44,688
[Edward clucks]

377
00:21:47,180 --> 00:21:48,408
[Edward grunts]

378
00:21:51,500 --> 00:21:52,979
[Edward gasps]

379
00:21:54,300 --> 00:21:55,699
What a rush!

380
00:21:57,580 --> 00:21:59,411
What the hell just happened?

381
00:21:59,500 --> 00:22:00,694
[Sighs]

382
00:22:01,780 --> 00:22:04,010
A very surprising side effect.

383
00:22:04,860 --> 00:22:07,613
While you were mesmerized
by my 3-D TV...

384
00:22:08,660 --> 00:22:11,413
...I utilized your neural energy
to grow smarter.

385
00:22:11,540 --> 00:22:13,371
Bruce Wayne was right!

386
00:22:14,140 --> 00:22:16,859
STICKLEY: You demented, bizarre,
unethical toad!

387
00:22:17,500 --> 00:22:19,377
It is brain manipulation!

388
00:22:19,460 --> 00:22:21,849
STICKLEY: I'm reporting you to the FCC!
EDWARD: Oh!

389
00:22:21,940 --> 00:22:24,579
STICKLEY: The human
experimentation board! The AMI!

390
00:22:24,660 --> 00:22:25,854
- And the police!
- Eee!

391
00:22:25,940 --> 00:22:27,931
STICKLEY: You are going up on charges...

392
00:22:28,020 --> 00:22:29,135
...to court, to jail...

393
00:22:29,220 --> 00:22:30,209
[Edward hums]

394
00:22:30,300 --> 00:22:33,258
...and then to a mental institution
for the rest of your life!

395
00:22:33,340 --> 00:22:35,808
But, first and foremost,
Nygma, you are fired!

396
00:22:35,900 --> 00:22:37,811
[Yells] Do you hear me? Fired!

397
00:22:39,900 --> 00:22:40,889
Ooohh...

398
00:22:43,380 --> 00:22:45,018
I don't think so.

399
00:22:46,660 --> 00:22:47,888
[Edward grunts]

400
00:22:48,180 --> 00:22:49,659
[Stickley screams]

401
00:22:54,100 --> 00:22:55,215
[Screams]

402
00:22:56,180 --> 00:22:57,249
[Crash]

403
00:22:58,300 --> 00:22:59,528
STICKLEY: Help!

404
00:22:59,700 --> 00:23:00,689
Whoa!

405
00:23:00,940 --> 00:23:01,929
[Sobbing]

406
00:23:02,020 --> 00:23:03,499
[Roaring vibrations]

407
00:23:03,580 --> 00:23:05,298
EDWARD: [Shrieks] Hang on!

408
00:23:06,100 --> 00:23:07,294
[Both gasping]

409
00:23:09,340 --> 00:23:10,455
Babe!

410
00:23:10,900 --> 00:23:12,379
You are fired!

411
00:23:12,980 --> 00:23:14,698
EDWARD: Or should I say...

412
00:23:15,340 --> 00:23:16,534
...terminated?

413
00:23:18,620 --> 00:23:20,497
[Stickley's screaming echoes]

414
00:23:21,660 --> 00:23:23,571
[Yells] Surf's up, Big Kahuna!

415
00:23:25,260 --> 00:23:26,010
[Crash]

416
00:23:26,100 --> 00:23:27,089
Oohhh!

417
00:23:27,700 --> 00:23:29,930
Nice form, but rough on the landing.

418
00:23:30,100 --> 00:23:32,694
He may have to settle for the Bronze.

419
00:23:32,780 --> 00:23:34,293
[Cackles hysterically]

420
00:23:37,340 --> 00:23:39,137
"Questions," Mr. Wayne?

421
00:23:40,380 --> 00:23:42,814
My work raises too many questions?

422
00:23:43,860 --> 00:23:45,657
<i>Why hasn't anybody...</i>

423
00:23:47,380 --> 00:23:49,530
<i>[Whispers] ... put you in your place?</i>

424
00:23:51,180 --> 00:23:53,899
<i>NEWSCASTER: Harvey Dent,
once Gotham's District Attorney...</i>

425
00:23:53,980 --> 00:23:57,256
<i>... was horribly scarred
by underworld kingpin, Boss Moroni.</i>

426
00:23:57,340 --> 00:23:59,535
<i>Although Batman tried to save him...</i>

427
00:23:59,740 --> 00:24:03,449
<i>... Dent's left-brain damage
turned him into a violent criminal...</i>

428
00:24:03,540 --> 00:24:06,134
<i>... who blamed Batman
and who has vowed to destroy him.</i>

429
00:24:06,220 --> 00:24:07,335
[Alfred talks on phone]

430
00:24:07,420 --> 00:24:10,651
<i>Harvey Two-Face is extremely dangerous,
repeat, extremely dangerous.</i>

431
00:24:10,740 --> 00:24:12,492
That was the Commissioner.

432
00:24:12,660 --> 00:24:15,652
There's been an accident
at Wayne Enterprises.

433
00:24:17,100 --> 00:24:18,818
BRUCE: Horrible way to die.

434
00:24:18,900 --> 00:24:20,970
The surveillance cameras are down here.

435
00:24:21,060 --> 00:24:25,099
We'll dredge the river, but with
that current, I doubt we'll find the body.

436
00:24:26,180 --> 00:24:28,410
[Soft instrumental music, background]

437
00:24:28,500 --> 00:24:29,569
Why?

438
00:24:29,820 --> 00:24:31,048
Oh, why?

439
00:24:31,740 --> 00:24:32,729
[Sobs]

440
00:24:33,820 --> 00:24:35,697
I just can't believe it.

441
00:24:35,980 --> 00:24:38,574
Two years working in the same office.

442
00:24:39,380 --> 00:24:41,211
He was like my father...

443
00:24:41,340 --> 00:24:42,659
...my brother...

444
00:24:42,740 --> 00:24:44,537
...or a cousin that visits a lot.

445
00:24:44,620 --> 00:24:45,609
[Sobs]

446
00:24:45,700 --> 00:24:47,418
Get a grip, Edward.

447
00:24:49,300 --> 00:24:51,018
I found this in my cubicle.

448
00:24:51,100 --> 00:24:55,378
You'll find the handwriting matches his,
as does the sentence structure.

449
00:24:59,020 --> 00:25:01,614
I couldn't possibly continue on here.

450
00:25:02,860 --> 00:25:04,452
[Gasps] The memories...

451
00:25:06,420 --> 00:25:08,809
BRUCE: This is last night's security log.

452
00:25:09,300 --> 00:25:10,733
<i>There's Stickley.</i>

453
00:25:11,820 --> 00:25:13,094
[Stickley laughing]

454
00:25:13,180 --> 00:25:14,249
[Crash]

455
00:25:16,540 --> 00:25:18,132
Pretty cut and dry.

456
00:25:23,900 --> 00:25:25,856
Yes, definitely suicide.

457
00:25:27,100 --> 00:25:30,251
Thanks very much for your help, Bruce.
We'll be in touch.

458
00:25:33,620 --> 00:25:38,136
BRUCE: Stickley's suicide doesn't make
sense. I want full benefits for his family.

459
00:25:38,300 --> 00:25:40,894
Suicide's not covered
by our corporate insurance policy.

460
00:25:40,980 --> 00:25:42,572
I know. Full benefits.

461
00:25:42,740 --> 00:25:46,574
Gossip Gerty called 32 times.
Who are you taking to the Charity Circus?

462
00:25:46,740 --> 00:25:49,049
BRUCE: I'll let you know. What's this?

463
00:25:49,460 --> 00:25:50,654
I don't know.

464
00:25:50,740 --> 00:25:52,492
I didn't see anyone.

465
00:26:01,460 --> 00:26:04,179
BRUCE: "If you look at the numbers
on my face...

466
00:26:04,300 --> 00:26:06,575
"...you won't find 13 anyplace."

467
00:26:07,060 --> 00:26:08,288
That's hideous.

468
00:26:08,580 --> 00:26:10,218
MARGARET: What does it mean?

469
00:26:10,300 --> 00:26:11,449
It's a riddle.

470
00:26:11,540 --> 00:26:13,576
"Numbers on my face... 13."

471
00:26:14,460 --> 00:26:15,893
One through twelve.

472
00:26:16,020 --> 00:26:17,612
The answer is a clock.

473
00:26:17,740 --> 00:26:19,856
Who would send you a riddle?

474
00:26:20,380 --> 00:26:21,608
That, Maggie...

475
00:26:21,820 --> 00:26:23,253
...is the riddle.

476
00:26:29,340 --> 00:26:30,978
[Pop song begins]

477
00:26:39,140 --> 00:26:41,256
<i>"You're sort of stuck where you are</i>

478
00:26:43,380 --> 00:26:44,859
<i>"Where in your dreams</i>

479
00:26:45,340 --> 00:26:47,092
<i>"You can buy expensive cars</i>

480
00:26:51,300 --> 00:26:52,892
<i>"Or live on Mars</i>

481
00:26:53,460 --> 00:26:55,257
<i>"And have it your way"</i>

482
00:27:00,580 --> 00:27:02,491
[Riddler doll chuckles]

483
00:27:02,660 --> 00:27:04,651
<i>"You hate your boss at your job"</i>

484
00:27:05,740 --> 00:27:07,378
Guess what I did today?

485
00:27:07,460 --> 00:27:09,052
<i>"But in your dreams</i>

486
00:27:09,420 --> 00:27:11,411
<i>"You can blow his head off</i>

487
00:27:14,820 --> 00:27:16,333
<i>"In your dreams</i>

488
00:27:16,580 --> 00:27:17,808
<i>"Show no mercy"</i>

489
00:27:19,700 --> 00:27:21,611
[Riddler doll chuckles]

490
00:27:25,260 --> 00:27:26,898
[Motorcycle engine revs]

491
00:27:29,140 --> 00:27:31,574
[Dramatic instrumental music, background]

492
00:27:33,500 --> 00:27:34,979
EDWARD: Wayne Manor.

493
00:27:36,980 --> 00:27:37,969
Humph!

494
00:27:44,460 --> 00:27:45,893
See you soon.

495
00:27:58,420 --> 00:28:00,058
[Ambient traffic sounds]

496
00:28:06,700 --> 00:28:09,578
[Dramatic instrumental music continues,
background]

497
00:28:15,660 --> 00:28:18,049
BRUCE: Dr. Meridian, please. Thank you.

498
00:28:29,180 --> 00:28:31,011
[Chase gasping and groaning]

499
00:28:33,260 --> 00:28:34,329
[Rattling]

500
00:28:41,420 --> 00:28:42,614
[Chase gasps]

501
00:28:44,300 --> 00:28:45,938
[Chase breathes heavily]

502
00:28:48,060 --> 00:28:50,016
[Stutters] I... guess I'm early.

503
00:28:51,500 --> 00:28:53,092
I have an appointment.

504
00:28:53,300 --> 00:28:54,653
I'm Bruce Wayne.

505
00:28:55,220 --> 00:28:56,335
Good.

506
00:28:56,580 --> 00:28:59,014
Then you can afford to buy me a new door.

507
00:28:59,580 --> 00:29:00,854
I'm sorry.

508
00:29:04,700 --> 00:29:07,089
BRUCE: You... sounded like you were in...

509
00:29:11,980 --> 00:29:13,652
...you know, trouble.

510
00:29:14,820 --> 00:29:18,449
I prefer healthy expressions of violence
as opposed to breaking in.

511
00:29:19,740 --> 00:29:20,889
CHASE: So...

512
00:29:21,140 --> 00:29:22,971
...how can I help you?

513
00:29:25,740 --> 00:29:28,413
Someone's been sending me love letters.

514
00:29:28,740 --> 00:29:31,254
One at my office and one at my home.

515
00:29:33,060 --> 00:29:36,496
Commissioner Gordon thought
you might give me your opinion.

516
00:29:41,500 --> 00:29:42,694
A clock.

517
00:29:42,860 --> 00:29:43,815
Clock.

518
00:29:46,980 --> 00:29:49,414
CHASE: "Tear one off and scratch my head.

519
00:29:50,860 --> 00:29:53,454
"What once was red is black instead."

520
00:29:55,700 --> 00:29:56,928
A match.

521
00:30:01,860 --> 00:30:04,328
My opinion: this letter writer is a wacko.

522
00:30:04,860 --> 00:30:05,895
"Wacko?"

523
00:30:06,460 --> 00:30:08,132
Is that a technical term?

524
00:30:08,620 --> 00:30:11,134
Patient may suffer from obsession...

525
00:30:11,340 --> 00:30:15,174
...with potential homicidal tendencies.
Is that better for you?

526
00:30:15,500 --> 00:30:17,172
So, what you're saying is...

527
00:30:17,260 --> 00:30:19,091
...this guy's a total wacko.

528
00:30:19,180 --> 00:30:20,408
CHASE: Exactly.

529
00:30:22,140 --> 00:30:23,732
He's obsessed with you.

530
00:30:23,820 --> 00:30:26,698
His only escape may be
to purge the fixation.

531
00:30:28,220 --> 00:30:29,414
To kill me.

532
00:30:30,060 --> 00:30:33,132
I think you understand obsession
better than you let on.

533
00:30:33,220 --> 00:30:36,132
<i>[Batman Forever theme song plays softly,
background]</i>

534
00:30:36,460 --> 00:30:37,734
You like bats?

535
00:30:38,820 --> 00:30:40,731
CHASE: That's a Rorschach, Mr. Wayne.

536
00:30:40,820 --> 00:30:42,173
An inkblot.

537
00:30:42,300 --> 00:30:43,972
People see what they want.

538
00:30:45,060 --> 00:30:47,528
CHASE: The question is: do you like bats?

539
00:30:49,860 --> 00:30:51,851
Still playing with dolls?

540
00:30:53,180 --> 00:30:55,455
CHASE: She's a Malaysian dream warden.

541
00:30:55,660 --> 00:30:58,697
Some cultures believe she protects you
from bad dreams.

542
00:30:59,500 --> 00:31:01,616
CHASE: It's silly to you, I'm sure.

543
00:31:06,100 --> 00:31:07,613
You look so sad.

544
00:31:09,100 --> 00:31:10,374
Do you need one?

545
00:31:11,140 --> 00:31:12,971
Me? No. Why would I?

546
00:31:15,300 --> 00:31:18,098
CHASE: You're not exactly what you seem,
are you?

547
00:31:19,420 --> 00:31:21,570
What is it you really came here for?

548
00:31:23,780 --> 00:31:25,418
Yikes, time's up.

549
00:31:27,460 --> 00:31:29,132
That's usually my line.

550
00:31:29,380 --> 00:31:31,291
BRUCE: I'd love to stay here chatting...

551
00:31:31,380 --> 00:31:32,699
Would you?

552
00:31:33,540 --> 00:31:34,814
I'm not so sure.

553
00:31:35,500 --> 00:31:37,934
I must get you out of those clothes.

554
00:31:38,900 --> 00:31:40,174
Excuse me?

555
00:31:40,300 --> 00:31:42,177
BRUCE: And into a black dress.

556
00:31:42,340 --> 00:31:44,934
Tell me, Doctor, do you like the circus?

557
00:31:51,900 --> 00:31:55,051
[Trumpets blare and drums pound
dramatic circus music]

558
00:32:02,780 --> 00:32:04,896
<i>RINGMASTER: Ladies and gentlemen...</i>

559
00:32:05,900 --> 00:32:07,970
<i>... boys and girls of all ages...</i>

560
00:32:08,100 --> 00:32:10,694
<i>... welcome to the greatest show on earth!</i>

561
00:32:10,860 --> 00:32:13,658
GOSSIP GERTY: Who is this beautiful
young woman you're with?

562
00:32:13,740 --> 00:32:15,093
BRUCE: Dr. Chase Meridian.

563
00:32:15,180 --> 00:32:16,295
GOSSIP GERTY: A doctor?

564
00:32:16,380 --> 00:32:17,972
What kind of doctor?

565
00:32:18,140 --> 00:32:20,415
<i>RINGMASTER ON TV:
... for Gotham Children's Hospital.</i>

566
00:32:20,500 --> 00:32:23,094
<i>Let's thank our largest single donor:</i>

567
00:32:23,780 --> 00:32:25,179
<i>Bruce Wayne!</i>

568
00:32:25,260 --> 00:32:26,852
[Applause on TV]

569
00:32:27,260 --> 00:32:29,649
<i>RINGMASTER ON TV:
Ladies and gentlemen...</i>

570
00:32:29,820 --> 00:32:31,890
<i>... 70 feet above the ground...</i>

571
00:32:32,060 --> 00:32:35,336
<i>... performing feats
of unimaginable aerial skill...</i>

572
00:32:35,940 --> 00:32:37,851
<i>... the Flying Graysons!</i>

573
00:32:41,540 --> 00:32:44,134
[Dramatic circus music
with rhythmic drumbeat]

574
00:32:44,220 --> 00:32:45,733
[Thunderous applause]

575
00:33:03,180 --> 00:33:05,250
[Applause and cheering continue]

576
00:33:16,860 --> 00:33:19,090
[Cries of astonishment from audience]

577
00:33:26,340 --> 00:33:28,251
[Applause and cheering]

578
00:33:30,060 --> 00:33:31,015
Listen...

579
00:33:31,100 --> 00:33:34,729
...I'm going rock climbing this weekend.
Would you like to join me?

580
00:33:34,820 --> 00:33:35,809
Um...

581
00:33:35,940 --> 00:33:37,339
...I'd like to.

582
00:33:37,580 --> 00:33:40,048
I love climbing. I really love it.

583
00:33:40,460 --> 00:33:41,290
But?

584
00:33:42,060 --> 00:33:43,413
I've met someone.

585
00:33:44,620 --> 00:33:46,975
That's fast work. You just moved here.

586
00:33:47,180 --> 00:33:48,772
You could say he just...

587
00:33:48,900 --> 00:33:51,209
...dropped out of the sky and...

588
00:33:51,660 --> 00:33:52,695
...bang!

589
00:33:54,220 --> 00:33:55,858
I think he felt it too.

590
00:33:55,980 --> 00:33:57,129
He sure did.

591
00:33:57,340 --> 00:33:58,216
What?

592
00:33:59,980 --> 00:34:01,174
Who wouldn't?

593
00:34:02,540 --> 00:34:03,939
<i>RINGMASTER: Now...</i>

594
00:34:05,100 --> 00:34:06,169
<i>... Richard...</i>

595
00:34:06,260 --> 00:34:08,057
<i>... the youngest Flying Grayson...</i>

596
00:34:08,140 --> 00:34:09,334
[Applause]

597
00:34:09,420 --> 00:34:11,570
<i>... will perform the awe-inspiring...</i>

598
00:34:11,660 --> 00:34:12,979
<i>... death drop...</i>

599
00:34:13,060 --> 00:34:14,254
CROWD: Whoa!

600
00:34:14,580 --> 00:34:16,457
<i>RINGMASTER: ... without the safety...</i>

601
00:34:16,540 --> 00:34:17,689
<i>... of a net!</i>

602
00:34:19,180 --> 00:34:20,249
[Applause]

603
00:34:35,780 --> 00:34:37,293
DAD GRAYSON: Let's go.

604
00:34:37,380 --> 00:34:39,211
MOM GRAYSON: You'll be okay.

605
00:34:42,300 --> 00:34:44,530
[Cries of astonishment from audience]

606
00:34:54,860 --> 00:34:56,179
[Groaning]

607
00:34:56,260 --> 00:34:58,171
[Applause and cheering]

608
00:35:05,460 --> 00:35:07,894
[Dramatic instrumental music, background]

609
00:35:12,180 --> 00:35:13,659
<i>TWO-FACE: Ladies...</i>

610
00:35:13,740 --> 00:35:15,219
<i>... and gentlemen!</i>

611
00:35:16,340 --> 00:35:19,855
<i>Now, the new management
of the circus invites you to forget...</i>

612
00:35:20,020 --> 00:35:22,250
<i>... this good, wholesome fun...</i>

613
00:35:22,460 --> 00:35:25,020
<i>... and join us in a celebration
of absolute chaos...</i>

614
00:35:25,100 --> 00:35:26,579
<i>... and true jesters!</i>

615
00:35:27,740 --> 00:35:29,139
<i>Bring it on!</i>

616
00:35:29,660 --> 00:35:30,615
<i>Now!</i>

617
00:35:31,420 --> 00:35:33,650
[Yelling and screaming from audience]

618
00:35:36,140 --> 00:35:37,732
[Eerie cackling on TV]

619
00:35:39,180 --> 00:35:40,852
[Laughs excitedly]

620
00:35:41,740 --> 00:35:43,970
<i>Tonight, a new act for your...</i>

621
00:35:44,100 --> 00:35:47,888
<i>... personal amazement.
We call it, "Massacre under the Big Top."</i>

622
00:35:47,980 --> 00:35:49,049
[Cackles]

623
00:35:49,580 --> 00:35:52,458
<i>TWO-FACE: Let us direct your attention
to the ring.</i>

624
00:35:53,180 --> 00:35:55,694
<i>Inside this harmless-looking orb are two...</i>

625
00:35:56,660 --> 00:35:59,174
<i>... that's two hundred sticks of TNT.</i>

626
00:36:00,300 --> 00:36:02,370
<i>And in our innocent hand...</i>

627
00:36:02,580 --> 00:36:04,377
<i>... a radio detonator.</i>

628
00:36:05,100 --> 00:36:06,738
MAYOR: What do you want?

629
00:36:06,900 --> 00:36:08,458
<i>Want, Mr. Mayor?</i>

630
00:36:08,660 --> 00:36:10,491
<i>TWO-FACE: One simple thing: Batman.</i>

631
00:36:10,580 --> 00:36:12,491
<i>Bruised, broken, bleeding...</i>

632
00:36:12,660 --> 00:36:14,298
<i>[Yells] ... in a word: dead!</i>

633
00:36:14,380 --> 00:36:15,893
[Laughs hysterically]

634
00:36:18,620 --> 00:36:19,575
Batman.

635
00:36:20,260 --> 00:36:22,171
<i>TWO-FACE: Who do we have before us?</i>

636
00:36:22,260 --> 00:36:23,852
<i>[Whispers] Gotham's finest...</i>

637
00:36:23,940 --> 00:36:25,055
<i>... well-to-do...</i>

638
00:36:25,140 --> 00:36:26,209
<i>... influential.</i>

639
00:36:26,300 --> 00:36:28,575
<i>Surely one of you knows who Batman is.</i>

640
00:36:28,660 --> 00:36:31,493
<i>Hell, odds are one of you pasty-faced twits
is Batman!</i>

641
00:36:31,580 --> 00:36:33,013
[Screams from audience]

642
00:36:33,100 --> 00:36:34,897
<i>You have two minutes.</i>

643
00:36:37,700 --> 00:36:38,689
[Ticking]

644
00:36:41,220 --> 00:36:42,539
[Shouts] Harvey!

645
00:36:43,140 --> 00:36:44,493
I'm Batman!

646
00:36:46,180 --> 00:36:48,455
[Chaotic yelling and screaming]

647
00:36:50,700 --> 00:36:51,610
Bruce!

648
00:36:51,740 --> 00:36:53,378
[Hooting and hollering]

649
00:36:55,100 --> 00:36:57,773
[Dramatic instrumental music, background]

650
00:36:58,980 --> 00:37:00,732
[Chaotic yelling continues]

651
00:37:01,060 --> 00:37:02,129
[Grunting]

652
00:37:02,900 --> 00:37:03,969
We can stop them.

653
00:37:04,060 --> 00:37:05,379
DAD GRAYSON: Go out on the rigging.

654
00:37:05,460 --> 00:37:06,176
Be careful.

655
00:37:06,260 --> 00:37:07,409
Don't worry.

656
00:37:07,500 --> 00:37:09,138
[Grunting and groaning]

657
00:37:18,580 --> 00:37:21,458
[Dramatic instrumental music continues,
background]

658
00:37:21,740 --> 00:37:23,378
[Screams from audience]

659
00:37:24,620 --> 00:37:26,258
TWO-FACE: Go to work, boys!

660
00:37:26,340 --> 00:37:27,614
[Cackles]

661
00:37:34,820 --> 00:37:35,809
[Ticking]

662
00:37:45,460 --> 00:37:46,654
[Laughs]

663
00:37:47,340 --> 00:37:48,932
Our kind of day.

664
00:37:57,700 --> 00:37:59,850
MOM GRAYSON: Reach for it! Stop it!

665
00:38:00,660 --> 00:38:02,298
[Grunting and groaning]

666
00:38:02,580 --> 00:38:04,298
[Rapid machine-gun blasts]

667
00:38:05,260 --> 00:38:06,329
Oh, my God.

668
00:38:06,620 --> 00:38:07,973
[Screaming]

669
00:38:08,180 --> 00:38:09,454
[Ticking]

670
00:38:13,580 --> 00:38:15,491
[Grunting and groaning]

671
00:38:18,660 --> 00:38:20,298
[Two-Face laughs]

672
00:38:24,740 --> 00:38:25,934
[Shrieks]

673
00:38:31,500 --> 00:38:32,489
[Ticking]

674
00:38:34,380 --> 00:38:35,449
[Grunts]

675
00:38:42,540 --> 00:38:43,893
[Explosion]

676
00:38:48,140 --> 00:38:51,098
[Melancholic instrumental melody plays,
background]

677
00:39:02,260 --> 00:39:03,249
[Sobs]

678
00:39:42,860 --> 00:39:45,897
It's good you took him in.
He hasn't anyone now.

679
00:39:46,060 --> 00:39:49,530
He's filled out papers all day.
He hasn't slept or eaten.

680
00:40:00,900 --> 00:40:02,572
ALFRED: Welcome, Master Grayson.

681
00:40:02,660 --> 00:40:03,775
I'm Alfred.

682
00:40:04,220 --> 00:40:05,733
How're you doing, Al?

683
00:40:07,100 --> 00:40:11,332
BRUCE: There's a room prepared for you.
But perhaps you'd like to eat first.

684
00:40:13,580 --> 00:40:15,411
Okay, I'm out of here.

685
00:40:17,260 --> 00:40:18,295
Excuse me?

686
00:40:18,380 --> 00:40:20,530
Telling that cop I'd stay here...

687
00:40:20,740 --> 00:40:23,777
...saved me a lot
of social-service interviews.

688
00:40:24,140 --> 00:40:26,529
So, no offense, but no thanks. See you.

689
00:40:26,820 --> 00:40:28,219
DICK: Take it easy.

690
00:40:39,300 --> 00:40:43,009
BRUCE: Where will you go?
The circus must be halfway to Metropolis.

691
00:40:43,180 --> 00:40:44,852
DICK: Get a fix on Two-Face.

692
00:40:44,940 --> 00:40:46,339
Then I'll kill him.

693
00:40:46,860 --> 00:40:49,374
Killing Two-Face won't take the pain away.

694
00:40:49,580 --> 00:40:51,059
BRUCE: It'll make it worse.

695
00:40:51,140 --> 00:40:53,096
Spare me the sermons, all right?

696
00:40:53,860 --> 00:40:56,294
DICK: I don't need your advice
or your charity.

697
00:40:56,380 --> 00:40:57,813
[Motorcycle engine revs]

698
00:40:57,900 --> 00:40:59,128
Nice bike.

699
00:40:59,340 --> 00:41:01,649
Hang out at a lot of biker bars?

700
00:41:04,100 --> 00:41:06,011
You're almost on empty.

701
00:41:06,180 --> 00:41:09,411
Fill it up in the garage.
There's no gas station for miles.

702
00:41:16,940 --> 00:41:18,453
BRUCE: The pump's over here.

703
00:41:18,540 --> 00:41:21,134
DICK: Is this a garage or a car museum,
Bruce?

704
00:41:23,940 --> 00:41:25,009
DICK: Wow!

705
00:41:29,860 --> 00:41:31,373
DICK: That's a 1917 Harley.

706
00:41:31,460 --> 00:41:32,575
BRUCE: Yep.

707
00:41:32,780 --> 00:41:35,055
DICK: Indian Classic, fully restored.

708
00:41:35,820 --> 00:41:37,776
This is a Vincent Black Knight.

709
00:41:38,340 --> 00:41:39,898
They only made a hundred.

710
00:41:39,980 --> 00:41:42,653
A hundred and one, actually.
She's my favorite.

711
00:41:43,020 --> 00:41:44,453
You've got two.

712
00:41:44,620 --> 00:41:46,133
That one doesn't run.

713
00:41:46,860 --> 00:41:49,135
BRUCE: The throttle sticks on this one.

714
00:41:49,220 --> 00:41:51,336
Alfred's a good mechanic, but...

715
00:41:51,780 --> 00:41:53,657
<i>... these need a lot of work.</i>

716
00:41:54,180 --> 00:41:55,898
<i>If someone were to fix them up...</i>

717
00:41:55,980 --> 00:41:57,618
...they could keep one.

718
00:41:59,460 --> 00:42:00,654
BRUCE: Anyway...

719
00:42:00,740 --> 00:42:02,219
...have a nice trip.

720
00:42:02,860 --> 00:42:04,532
You'll land on your feet.

721
00:42:07,820 --> 00:42:09,970
Is the young master leaving?

722
00:42:10,220 --> 00:42:11,335
Pity.

723
00:42:11,500 --> 00:42:15,175
I'll just toss this away then.
Perhaps the dogs are hungry.

724
00:42:18,620 --> 00:42:20,258
Hey, Al, wait up.

725
00:42:23,340 --> 00:42:25,615
[Soft instrumental music, background]

726
00:42:51,060 --> 00:42:52,971
[Faint sound of voices]

727
00:42:55,340 --> 00:42:57,456
[Distorted sound of gunshot]

728
00:43:03,580 --> 00:43:05,571
[Distorted sound of gunshot]

729
00:43:20,180 --> 00:43:21,818
[Thunder rumbles]

730
00:43:24,180 --> 00:43:26,171
[Priest reciting prayers]

731
00:43:44,740 --> 00:43:47,618
[Melancholic instrumental melody plays,
background]

732
00:44:09,220 --> 00:44:10,733
ALFRED: Master Bruce?

733
00:44:13,500 --> 00:44:14,933
<i>Master Bruce?</i>

734
00:44:15,740 --> 00:44:17,537
Just like my parents.

735
00:44:18,260 --> 00:44:19,932
It's happening again.

736
00:44:20,820 --> 00:44:24,256
A monster comes out of the night,
a scream, two shots.

737
00:44:26,100 --> 00:44:27,453
I killed them.

738
00:44:27,860 --> 00:44:29,452
What did you say?

739
00:44:29,780 --> 00:44:30,895
He killed them.

740
00:44:30,980 --> 00:44:32,129
Two-Face.

741
00:44:32,420 --> 00:44:34,570
He slaughtered that boy's parents.

742
00:44:34,740 --> 00:44:35,934
ALFRED: No, no.

743
00:44:36,380 --> 00:44:38,416
You said, "I killed them."

744
00:44:45,140 --> 00:44:47,131
[Sirens blaring in distance]

745
00:44:50,380 --> 00:44:51,938
Take care of the kid.

746
00:44:52,220 --> 00:44:53,539
Certainly, sir.

747
00:44:59,620 --> 00:45:00,735
[Footsteps]

748
00:45:01,340 --> 00:45:04,093
ALFRED: Can I help you settle in,
Master Grayson?

749
00:45:04,580 --> 00:45:05,615
DICK: No.

750
00:45:05,940 --> 00:45:07,931
Thanks, I won't be staying long.

751
00:45:08,020 --> 00:45:10,898
[Melancholic instrumental melody plays,
background]

752
00:45:10,980 --> 00:45:12,572
Is this a robin?

753
00:45:15,620 --> 00:45:19,169
My brother's wire broke once
and I swung out and grabbed him.

754
00:45:20,580 --> 00:45:22,730
DICK: My father said I was his hero.

755
00:45:23,980 --> 00:45:25,891
I flew in like a robin.

756
00:45:28,340 --> 00:45:30,410
Some hero I turned out to be.

757
00:45:31,300 --> 00:45:33,336
But your father was right.

758
00:45:33,540 --> 00:45:35,690
You are a hero. I can tell.

759
00:45:42,580 --> 00:45:45,777
Throw this away, will you?
I won't need it anymore.

760
00:45:48,300 --> 00:45:50,689
ALFRED: I think I'll just put it in here.

761
00:45:56,900 --> 00:45:58,936
Broken wings mend in time.

762
00:46:00,460 --> 00:46:02,655
One day Robin will fly again.

763
00:46:03,140 --> 00:46:04,289
I promise.

764
00:46:11,580 --> 00:46:13,536
[Batmobile engine roars]

765
00:46:17,260 --> 00:46:19,820
<i>[Batman Forever theme song plays,
background]</i>

766
00:46:25,740 --> 00:46:27,492
[Engines accelerate]

767
00:46:29,620 --> 00:46:30,939
[Thug cackles]

768
00:46:33,980 --> 00:46:35,652
[Carriage rattles]

769
00:46:43,700 --> 00:46:44,974
[Cackles]

770
00:46:48,980 --> 00:46:49,935
[Beep]

771
00:46:50,660 --> 00:46:52,013
[Explosive blast]

772
00:46:53,220 --> 00:46:54,573
[Shrieking]

773
00:46:56,060 --> 00:46:57,778
[Roaring explosion]

774
00:47:00,860 --> 00:47:02,054
[Moans]

775
00:47:03,060 --> 00:47:04,698
[Tires squealing]

776
00:47:06,980 --> 00:47:09,540
[Fast-paced instrumental rhythm,
background]

777
00:47:13,060 --> 00:47:14,413
[Two-Face groans]

778
00:47:23,540 --> 00:47:24,814
TWO-FACE: We'll drive.

779
00:47:24,900 --> 00:47:26,936
[Rapid machine-gun blasts]

780
00:47:30,660 --> 00:47:31,934
[Cackles]

781
00:47:38,500 --> 00:47:40,138
[Tires squealing]

782
00:47:44,460 --> 00:47:46,337
[Rapid machine-gun blasts]

783
00:47:46,420 --> 00:47:47,489
[Cackles]

784
00:47:57,700 --> 00:47:59,736
[Rapid machine-gun blasts]

785
00:48:03,060 --> 00:48:06,018
[Fast-paced instrumental rhythm
continues, background]

786
00:48:09,260 --> 00:48:11,057
[Mechanical clanking]

787
00:48:14,140 --> 00:48:16,096
[Batmobile engine roars]

788
00:48:20,820 --> 00:48:22,173
[Explosion]

789
00:48:24,180 --> 00:48:25,374
[Gasps]

790
00:48:27,940 --> 00:48:29,532
[Music climaxes]

791
00:48:40,300 --> 00:48:41,619
[Two-Face wails]

792
00:48:46,060 --> 00:48:47,698
[Electronic beeping]

793
00:48:54,140 --> 00:48:55,289
The Puzzler?

794
00:48:55,380 --> 00:48:57,052
[Low-pitched buzzing]

795
00:48:57,940 --> 00:48:59,419
[Electronic beeping]

796
00:49:00,220 --> 00:49:01,414
The Gamester?

797
00:49:01,900 --> 00:49:03,697
[Low-pitched buzzing]

798
00:49:08,300 --> 00:49:09,653
Captain Kill?

799
00:49:09,740 --> 00:49:11,253
[Low-pitched buzzing]

800
00:49:13,660 --> 00:49:15,298
EDWARD: Question Mark Man?

801
00:49:15,380 --> 00:49:16,369
[Electronic beeping]

802
00:49:16,460 --> 00:49:17,893
EDWARD: No, no, no!

803
00:49:18,220 --> 00:49:19,539
[High-pitched ringing]

804
00:49:19,620 --> 00:49:20,814
[Sighs]

805
00:49:25,180 --> 00:49:27,091
[Riddler doll chuckles]

806
00:49:29,060 --> 00:49:30,891
[High-pitched ringing]

807
00:49:32,780 --> 00:49:35,010
Thank you. Thank you so much.

808
00:49:35,100 --> 00:49:36,419
[Giggling]

809
00:49:37,300 --> 00:49:39,973
[Dramatic instrumental music, background]

810
00:49:41,620 --> 00:49:42,939
[Sirens blaring]

811
00:49:48,380 --> 00:49:51,053
The Bat's stubborn refusal to expire...

812
00:49:52,540 --> 00:49:54,496
...is driving us insane!

813
00:49:57,660 --> 00:49:59,332
Don't worry, baby.

814
00:49:59,420 --> 00:50:00,648
[Spice giggles]

815
00:50:00,860 --> 00:50:02,657
You'll kill him soon.

816
00:50:07,260 --> 00:50:08,579
Besides...

817
00:50:08,940 --> 00:50:10,771
...I made your favorite:

818
00:50:10,900 --> 00:50:12,811
Sparkling champagne and...

819
00:50:13,340 --> 00:50:16,093
...yummy poached salmon
with little quail eggs and...

820
00:50:16,180 --> 00:50:17,499
[Two-Face moans]

821
00:50:17,580 --> 00:50:18,979
...a creamy...

822
00:50:19,060 --> 00:50:20,254
...dreamy...

823
00:50:20,580 --> 00:50:22,218
...lemon soufflé.

824
00:50:22,780 --> 00:50:24,771
No, I made your favorite:

825
00:50:24,940 --> 00:50:27,249
A charred heart of black boar...

826
00:50:27,660 --> 00:50:29,935
...a side of raw donkey meat...

827
00:50:31,260 --> 00:50:34,616
...and a Sterno and grain alcohol,
straight up, baby!

828
00:50:34,700 --> 00:50:35,849
[AII laugh]

829
00:50:35,940 --> 00:50:37,339
TWO-FACE: Perfect!

830
00:50:37,580 --> 00:50:39,093
Ladies, you spoil us!

831
00:50:39,260 --> 00:50:41,899
We're of two minds about what to eat first.

832
00:50:42,060 --> 00:50:43,049
[Ding]

833
00:50:43,140 --> 00:50:44,016
What?

834
00:50:44,100 --> 00:50:45,931
RIDDLER: I hope you made extra.

835
00:50:46,020 --> 00:50:47,976
TWO-FACE: Who the hell are you?

836
00:50:48,580 --> 00:50:50,059
Just a friend.

837
00:50:50,340 --> 00:50:51,932
But you can call me...

838
00:50:52,580 --> 00:50:54,093
...The Riddler.

839
00:50:55,180 --> 00:50:56,295
[Riddler chuckles]

840
00:50:56,380 --> 00:51:00,089
I'll call you dead, is more like it!
How did you find us? Talk!

841
00:51:00,260 --> 00:51:04,572
But then if I talked, what would keep you
from slaying me, O Segregated One?

842
00:51:04,740 --> 00:51:08,096
That's never going to heal
if you don't stop picking.

843
00:51:09,540 --> 00:51:11,531
Let's see if you bleed green.

844
00:51:11,620 --> 00:51:12,575
Harvey!

845
00:51:12,660 --> 00:51:13,695
[Spice giggles]

846
00:51:13,780 --> 00:51:15,736
It's not me you want to kill.

847
00:51:16,060 --> 00:51:19,689
That's just too easy for someone
as powerful as you and...

848
00:51:20,220 --> 00:51:21,209
...you.

849
00:51:22,020 --> 00:51:23,009
But Batman...

850
00:51:23,100 --> 00:51:24,294
[Gasps]

851
00:51:24,740 --> 00:51:26,810
[Whispers]... there's a challenge.

852
00:51:26,980 --> 00:51:29,369
Kill the Bat! Sounds like a good idea.

853
00:51:29,980 --> 00:51:34,656
But have you thought it through? A few
bullets, a splash of blood, then what?

854
00:51:35,580 --> 00:51:36,899
Wet hands.

855
00:51:37,860 --> 00:51:39,896
Post-homicidal depression.

856
00:51:39,980 --> 00:51:41,299
[Whimpers]

857
00:51:44,020 --> 00:51:45,817
Why not humiliate him first?

858
00:51:45,940 --> 00:51:46,690
Yeah.

859
00:51:46,780 --> 00:51:50,295
RIDDLER: Expose his frailties.
Then, when he is at his weakest...

860
00:51:50,460 --> 00:51:52,018
[Shouts]... crush him!

861
00:51:54,180 --> 00:51:55,613
I see that...

862
00:51:55,940 --> 00:51:57,896
...sparkle in your left eye.

863
00:51:57,980 --> 00:51:59,174
[Two-Face chuckles]

864
00:51:59,260 --> 00:52:01,490
[Whispers] I can help you get Batman.

865
00:52:04,380 --> 00:52:05,859
That is, if you'II...

866
00:52:06,100 --> 00:52:08,694
...spare my life for just a few moments.

867
00:52:10,980 --> 00:52:12,333
[Two-Face grunts]

868
00:52:17,540 --> 00:52:18,734
[Sighs]

869
00:52:19,740 --> 00:52:21,014
Thank you.

870
00:52:21,700 --> 00:52:26,012
<i>I love what you've done with this place.
Heavy Metal meets House and Garden.</i>

871
00:52:27,740 --> 00:52:29,014
Beautiful.

872
00:52:29,140 --> 00:52:31,290
It's so dark and Gothic and...

873
00:52:31,780 --> 00:52:33,771
...disgustingly decadent.

874
00:52:33,860 --> 00:52:35,179
[Riddler snarls]

875
00:52:35,460 --> 00:52:37,894
RIDDLER: Yet so bright and chipper and...

876
00:52:39,580 --> 00:52:41,059
...conservative.

877
00:52:41,340 --> 00:52:42,614
[Whistles]

878
00:52:44,900 --> 00:52:46,413
RIDDLER: It's so you!

879
00:52:47,260 --> 00:52:48,852
[Sings] And yet, so you!

880
00:52:48,940 --> 00:52:50,009
[Chuckles]

881
00:52:51,300 --> 00:52:54,736
Very few people are both a summer
and a winter, but...

882
00:52:55,940 --> 00:52:57,817
...but you pull it off nicely.

883
00:52:57,900 --> 00:52:58,889
[Gunshot]

884
00:53:00,060 --> 00:53:01,698
What's the point?

885
00:53:02,660 --> 00:53:06,892
[Shouts] Has anyone ever told you, you
have a serious impulse-control problem?

886
00:53:07,180 --> 00:53:08,329
[Gun clicks]

887
00:53:08,580 --> 00:53:10,252
This is the point.

888
00:53:12,100 --> 00:53:13,931
[Electronic scanning sounds]

889
00:53:17,180 --> 00:53:20,013
[Fast-paced instrumental beat, background]

890
00:53:22,460 --> 00:53:24,416
This is how I found you.

891
00:53:24,820 --> 00:53:26,139
Let me demonstrate.

892
00:53:26,220 --> 00:53:27,209
[Zap]

893
00:53:27,660 --> 00:53:28,934
[Gasping]

894
00:53:32,260 --> 00:53:34,455
This is your brain on The Box.

895
00:53:34,660 --> 00:53:36,298
This is my brain on The Box.

896
00:53:36,380 --> 00:53:38,689
[Shrieks] Does anyone else feel
like a fried egg?

897
00:53:38,780 --> 00:53:39,929
I'll have more.

898
00:53:40,020 --> 00:53:41,009
[Pop]

899
00:53:41,100 --> 00:53:44,058
There's more. But only the first one's free.

900
00:53:44,900 --> 00:53:46,458
Here's the bargain:

901
00:53:46,620 --> 00:53:49,180
You'll help me steal production capital...

902
00:53:49,340 --> 00:53:52,059
...so I can put a Box on every TV in town...

903
00:53:52,220 --> 00:53:55,735
...and become Gotham's cleverest,
carbon-based life form!

904
00:53:57,060 --> 00:53:58,652
And in return...

905
00:54:00,540 --> 00:54:02,770
Is everybody paying attention?

906
00:54:02,980 --> 00:54:05,733
[Whispers] I will help you solve
the greatest riddle of all.

907
00:54:05,820 --> 00:54:07,856
The mother of all riddles:

908
00:54:09,340 --> 00:54:10,614
Who is...

909
00:54:11,100 --> 00:54:12,419
...Batman?

910
00:54:14,340 --> 00:54:16,410
You broke into our hideout.

911
00:54:16,660 --> 00:54:19,174
You violated the sanctity of our lair.

912
00:54:19,260 --> 00:54:21,820
We should crush your bones into powder.

913
00:54:21,980 --> 00:54:24,175
But you pose an interesting proposition.

914
00:54:24,260 --> 00:54:28,378
Therefore, heads: we accept,
and tails: we blow your damn head off.

915
00:54:33,700 --> 00:54:36,089
[People yelling and chattering excitedly]

916
00:54:38,180 --> 00:54:40,091
[Two-Face laughs hysterically]

917
00:54:43,260 --> 00:54:44,659
Here's a good one.

918
00:54:44,740 --> 00:54:46,253
TWO-FACE: No, no, no!

919
00:54:46,940 --> 00:54:48,692
There is a good one.

920
00:54:50,140 --> 00:54:54,019
- Leave that. I'll attend to it.
- I'm not used to being waited on.

921
00:55:18,300 --> 00:55:19,699
[Gasps] Don't shoot me!

922
00:55:19,780 --> 00:55:22,089
THUG: Don't eyeball me! Give me that!

923
00:55:22,180 --> 00:55:24,011
[Yelling and fighting]

924
00:55:25,380 --> 00:55:27,848
RIDDLER: Two-Face, show me how
to punch a guy!

925
00:55:27,940 --> 00:55:31,057
It's dead simple, my boy.
Ball up your fist, reach back...

926
00:55:31,140 --> 00:55:32,778
...and assert yourself.

927
00:55:34,340 --> 00:55:36,490
That looks fun. Let me try.

928
00:55:37,060 --> 00:55:40,370
Ball up the fist, reach way back...
assert yourself.

929
00:55:40,660 --> 00:55:41,695
Ow!

930
00:55:42,060 --> 00:55:45,018
[Fast-paced instrumental beat continues,
background]

931
00:55:45,180 --> 00:55:48,138
RIDDLER: One hundred thousand,
two hundred and twenty.

932
00:55:48,540 --> 00:55:49,973
One hundred and...

933
00:55:50,140 --> 00:55:51,573
[Shouts] I lost count!

934
00:55:51,660 --> 00:55:52,934
[Giggles excitedly]

935
00:55:53,140 --> 00:55:55,654
<i>FEMALE NEWSCASTER ON TV:
Last night another robbery...</i>

936
00:55:55,740 --> 00:55:57,731
<i>... perpetrated by
the Green-Suited Menace...</i>

937
00:55:57,820 --> 00:56:01,256
<i>... resulting in millions in diamonds stolen,
with no sign of Batman.</i>

938
00:56:01,340 --> 00:56:04,696
<i>MALE NEWSCASTER: Teamed with
Two-Face, this new criminal's pattern...</i>

939
00:56:04,780 --> 00:56:08,819
<i>... of marking his crimes with puzzles
has Gothamites calling him The Riddler.</i>

940
00:56:08,900 --> 00:56:11,937
Apparently, you and Batman
have a common enemy.

941
00:56:12,580 --> 00:56:14,491
That was with the morning mail.

942
00:56:16,500 --> 00:56:18,377
ALFRED: "The eight of us go forth,
not back.

943
00:56:18,460 --> 00:56:20,974
"To protect our king from the foe's attack."

944
00:56:22,300 --> 00:56:23,210
Chess pawns.

945
00:56:23,300 --> 00:56:24,335
Clock.

946
00:56:24,540 --> 00:56:25,211
Matches.

947
00:56:25,300 --> 00:56:27,052
All physical, man-made objects.

948
00:56:27,140 --> 00:56:29,370
ALFRED: Small in size, light in weight.

949
00:56:29,460 --> 00:56:30,779
What's the connection?

950
00:56:30,860 --> 00:56:34,489
ALFRED: With all due respect,
that's why they call him The Riddler.

951
00:56:34,980 --> 00:56:36,618
[Rattling and grunting]

952
00:56:36,980 --> 00:56:38,618
ALFRED: May I help you?

953
00:56:38,900 --> 00:56:41,050
Why is this the only locked door?

954
00:56:41,540 --> 00:56:43,212
What's back there?

955
00:56:43,380 --> 00:56:45,416
Master Wayne's dead wives.

956
00:56:46,660 --> 00:56:48,651
The silver closet. On your way.

957
00:56:52,100 --> 00:56:54,568
<i>EDWARD: Now, you can be part
of the action!</i>

958
00:56:54,660 --> 00:56:56,491
[Upbeat instrumental music, background]

959
00:56:56,580 --> 00:57:00,368
<i>Nygma Tech brings the joy
of 3-D entertainment into your home!</i>

960
00:57:00,660 --> 00:57:03,379
<i>Ladies and gentlemen, let me tell you...</i>

961
00:57:04,020 --> 00:57:05,453
<i>... my vision.</i>

962
00:57:06,740 --> 00:57:09,208
<i>The Box in every home in America...</i>

963
00:57:09,700 --> 00:57:11,213
<i>... and one day, the world!</i>

964
00:57:11,300 --> 00:57:12,494
[Crowd shouting]

965
00:57:12,580 --> 00:57:15,731
<i>FEMALE NEWSCASTER ON TV:
In local news, Edward Nygma's 3-D Box...</i>

966
00:57:15,820 --> 00:57:17,697
<i>... has become the rage of Gotham.</i>

967
00:57:17,780 --> 00:57:21,693
<i>Rioting occurred last night
at electronic stores that were sold out.</i>

968
00:57:22,100 --> 00:57:25,251
<i>There is hardly a home
without the Nygma Tech Box.</i>

969
00:57:25,980 --> 00:57:28,938
<i>Critics claim The Box turns Gothamites
into zombies.</i>

970
00:57:29,140 --> 00:57:30,778
<i>But Edward Nygma just shrugs.</i>

971
00:57:30,860 --> 00:57:33,738
<i>"That's what they said
when TV was invented. "</i>

972
00:57:33,820 --> 00:57:35,651
[Zapping and popping sounds]

973
00:57:42,340 --> 00:57:44,979
[Eerie instrumental music, background]

974
00:58:00,940 --> 00:58:02,771
[Riddler chuckles and gasps]

975
00:58:15,140 --> 00:58:16,619
ALFRED: Master Dick!

976
00:58:17,780 --> 00:58:18,974
DICK: Up here.

977
00:58:19,860 --> 00:58:21,851
Just checking, young sir.

978
00:58:26,940 --> 00:58:28,009
Now!

979
00:58:41,500 --> 00:58:42,774
[Yelling]

980
00:58:44,260 --> 00:58:45,329
[Clanking]

981
00:58:46,340 --> 00:58:47,409
[Groaning]

982
00:58:49,780 --> 00:58:52,340
<i>LOUDSPEAKER:
Intruder alert. Intruder alert.</i>

983
00:59:00,980 --> 00:59:03,414
[Dramatic instrumental music, background]

984
00:59:19,100 --> 00:59:21,978
CHASE: I have something for you.
It's on the table.

985
00:59:22,500 --> 00:59:24,013
<i>I hope you like it.</i>

986
00:59:34,380 --> 00:59:36,450
Call it clinical intuition.

987
00:59:37,300 --> 00:59:39,655
I thought your dreams needed changing.

988
00:59:42,700 --> 00:59:44,975
My parents were murdered before me...

989
00:59:45,180 --> 00:59:46,772
...when I was a kid.

990
00:59:49,660 --> 00:59:50,934
I don't...

991
00:59:51,460 --> 00:59:54,258
...remember a lot of what happened, but...

992
00:59:55,740 --> 00:59:58,777
...what I do comes to me in my dreams.
Flashes.

993
00:59:59,900 --> 01:00:03,210
There's a new element now, though,
I haven't seen before.

994
01:00:03,540 --> 01:00:05,496
It's a red leather book.

995
01:00:06,940 --> 01:00:08,612
Something else...

996
01:00:08,860 --> 01:00:11,533
BRUCE: My dreams come to me
when I'm awake now.

997
01:00:12,820 --> 01:00:15,698
Bruce, you're describing
repressed memories.

998
01:00:16,460 --> 01:00:19,770
CHASE: Images of a forgotten pain
that's trying to surface.

999
01:00:20,540 --> 01:00:22,098
[Tea-kettle hisses]

1000
01:00:22,740 --> 01:00:24,458
I'll be right back.

1001
01:00:43,820 --> 01:00:47,813
Is it possible there's an aspect
of your parents' death you haven't faced?

1002
01:00:47,980 --> 01:00:50,210
You were so young when it happened.

1003
01:00:51,580 --> 01:00:53,696
Maybe I should leave you two alone.

1004
01:00:55,020 --> 01:00:58,456
BRUCE: This goes way beyond taking
your work home, doesn't it?

1005
01:01:01,580 --> 01:01:02,933
CHASE: All right.

1006
01:01:04,620 --> 01:01:06,451
I think he's fascinating.

1007
01:01:07,100 --> 01:01:08,294
Clinically.

1008
01:01:08,700 --> 01:01:10,418
Why does a man do this?

1009
01:01:11,580 --> 01:01:13,969
It's as if he's cursed to pay a penance.

1010
01:01:14,140 --> 01:01:18,099
What crime could he have committed
to deserve a life of nightly torture?

1011
01:01:19,260 --> 01:01:20,852
It's more than just...

1012
01:01:21,740 --> 01:01:24,413
...professional interest, isn't it, Chase?

1013
01:01:25,340 --> 01:01:26,978
Bruce, are you jealous?

1014
01:01:27,700 --> 01:01:28,735
BRUCE: No.

1015
01:01:29,700 --> 01:01:31,895
I can't be jealous of Batman.

1016
01:01:33,220 --> 01:01:36,098
I want to be close,
but you won't let me near.

1017
01:01:37,860 --> 01:01:39,851
What are you protecting me from?

1018
01:01:41,180 --> 01:01:43,091
BRUCE: Do you want to know me?

1019
01:01:43,620 --> 01:01:45,497
Do you want to know who I am?

1020
01:01:47,340 --> 01:01:48,534
I guess...

1021
01:01:49,380 --> 01:01:51,177
...we're all two people.

1022
01:01:52,580 --> 01:01:55,777
BRUCE: The one in daylight,
and the one we keep in shadow.

1023
01:01:56,700 --> 01:01:57,894
Rage...

1024
01:01:58,140 --> 01:01:59,459
...violence...

1025
01:02:00,620 --> 01:02:01,735
...passion.

1026
01:02:02,820 --> 01:02:04,492
[Wristwatch beeps]

1027
01:02:05,820 --> 01:02:06,969
Excuse me.

1028
01:02:08,580 --> 01:02:09,695
I'm busy.

1029
01:02:09,860 --> 01:02:13,853
<i>I'm sorry to bother you.
I have some distressing news about Dick.</i>

1030
01:02:14,300 --> 01:02:15,335
Is he okay?

1031
01:02:15,420 --> 01:02:18,218
<i>I'm afraid Master Dick has gone traveling.</i>

1032
01:02:19,220 --> 01:02:20,619
BRUCE: He ran away?

1033
01:02:20,700 --> 01:02:22,736
<i>ALFRED: Actually, he took the car.</i>

1034
01:02:23,940 --> 01:02:25,373
He boosted the Jag?

1035
01:02:25,740 --> 01:02:26,934
<i>Not the Jaguar.</i>

1036
01:02:27,100 --> 01:02:28,419
<i>The other car.</i>

1037
01:02:28,620 --> 01:02:29,575
The Bentley?

1038
01:02:29,660 --> 01:02:30,854
<i>ALFRED: No, sir.</i>

1039
01:02:30,940 --> 01:02:32,419
<i>The other car.</i>

1040
01:02:35,100 --> 01:02:36,852
[Rock music blares, background]

1041
01:02:36,940 --> 01:02:38,134
[Tires squeal]

1042
01:02:39,260 --> 01:02:40,693
[Hoots and hollers]

1043
01:02:45,340 --> 01:02:47,137
[Crowd jeering and taunting]

1044
01:02:50,900 --> 01:02:52,458
[Rock music continues]

1045
01:02:55,580 --> 01:02:57,571
[Jeering and taunting continue]

1046
01:03:02,740 --> 01:03:05,538
Come for a little ride
in my love machine, babies?

1047
01:03:05,620 --> 01:03:06,973
[Hollering]

1048
01:03:10,900 --> 01:03:12,253
It's Batman!

1049
01:03:12,380 --> 01:03:14,052
WOMAN 1: Open up, Batman.

1050
01:03:15,660 --> 01:03:16,615
WOMAN 1: Wait!

1051
01:03:16,700 --> 01:03:18,099
That's not Batman!

1052
01:03:18,180 --> 01:03:19,499
What do you mean?

1053
01:03:19,580 --> 01:03:20,649
WOMAN 2: That's Batboy!

1054
01:03:20,740 --> 01:03:21,775
[AII laugh]

1055
01:03:21,860 --> 01:03:23,293
It ain't the Bat!

1056
01:03:23,380 --> 01:03:24,574
[Girl screams]

1057
01:03:27,060 --> 01:03:28,698
[Batmobile engine roars]

1058
01:03:36,540 --> 01:03:37,973
[Chaotic hollering]

1059
01:03:44,380 --> 01:03:45,449
DICK: Hey!

1060
01:03:45,620 --> 01:03:46,973
Let her go!

1061
01:03:47,060 --> 01:03:49,858
[Crowd snickers and groans sarcastically]

1062
01:03:52,620 --> 01:03:54,099
[Girl gasps and sobs]

1063
01:03:54,420 --> 01:03:56,012
Who the hell are you?

1064
01:03:56,500 --> 01:03:57,649
I'm Batman.

1065
01:03:57,740 --> 01:03:59,253
[Hysterical laughter]

1066
01:03:59,820 --> 01:04:01,970
I forgot my suit, all right?

1067
01:04:08,060 --> 01:04:09,971
[Grunting and groaning]

1068
01:04:30,340 --> 01:04:32,092
[Crazy Eddie grunts]

1069
01:04:34,300 --> 01:04:36,211
[Grunting and groaning]

1070
01:04:38,300 --> 01:04:39,449
[Girl gasps]

1071
01:04:40,540 --> 01:04:41,973
Come on, run!

1072
01:04:42,260 --> 01:04:44,455
Doesn't Batman ever kiss the girl?

1073
01:04:46,780 --> 01:04:47,496
DICK: Go!

1074
01:04:47,580 --> 01:04:49,411
GIRL: Thanks, you saved my life!

1075
01:04:49,500 --> 01:04:52,378
I could definitely get
into this superhero gig.

1076
01:04:52,540 --> 01:04:53,859
[Whistles]

1077
01:04:57,380 --> 01:04:59,018
[Riotous yelling]

1078
01:05:15,540 --> 01:05:16,734
CRAZY EDDIE: Batman!

1079
01:05:16,820 --> 01:05:19,618
[Dramatic instrumental music, background]

1080
01:05:29,940 --> 01:05:31,168
Bastard!

1081
01:05:31,540 --> 01:05:33,371
DICK: It should've been you!

1082
01:05:33,620 --> 01:05:36,930
[Gasps] If you had told Two-Face
who you were at the circus...

1083
01:05:37,020 --> 01:05:38,931
...they'd still be alive!

1084
01:05:41,940 --> 01:05:45,819
If Bruce Wayne could've given his life
for your family, he would have.

1085
01:05:45,900 --> 01:05:47,015
[Dick gasps]

1086
01:05:51,580 --> 01:05:54,731
DICK: All I can think about every day
is getting Two-Face.

1087
01:05:55,740 --> 01:05:57,492
He took my whole life.

1088
01:05:59,700 --> 01:06:01,531
When I was out there tonight...

1089
01:06:01,620 --> 01:06:03,770
...I imagined it was him I was fighting...

1090
01:06:03,860 --> 01:06:05,930
...even when I was fighting you...

1091
01:06:07,020 --> 01:06:08,738
...and the pain went away.

1092
01:06:10,140 --> 01:06:11,573
Do you understand?

1093
01:06:11,740 --> 01:06:13,093
BRUCE: Yes, I do.

1094
01:06:13,380 --> 01:06:14,335
Good.

1095
01:06:14,780 --> 01:06:16,657
You must help me find him.

1096
01:06:17,500 --> 01:06:18,853
DICK: When we do...

1097
01:06:18,940 --> 01:06:20,817
<i>... I'm the one who kills him.</i>

1098
01:06:22,140 --> 01:06:24,529
So, you're willing to take a life?

1099
01:06:25,460 --> 01:06:27,416
DICK: As long as it's Two-Face.

1100
01:06:29,980 --> 01:06:32,175
BRUCE: Then it will happen this way:

1101
01:06:33,340 --> 01:06:34,819
You make the kill.

1102
01:06:36,220 --> 01:06:39,212
But your pain doesn't die with Harvey,
it grows.

1103
01:06:39,380 --> 01:06:43,055
So you run into the night
to find another face, and another...

1104
01:06:43,580 --> 01:06:45,218
<i>... and another...</i>

1105
01:06:45,700 --> 01:06:48,976
<i>... until one terrible morning
you wake up and realize...</i>

1106
01:06:49,140 --> 01:06:51,700
...that revenge has become
your whole life...

1107
01:06:52,180 --> 01:06:53,852
...and you won't know why.

1108
01:06:55,060 --> 01:06:56,812
You can't understand.

1109
01:06:57,300 --> 01:06:59,575
Your family wasn't killed by a maniac.

1110
01:07:00,780 --> 01:07:02,293
Yes, they were.

1111
01:07:03,460 --> 01:07:05,018
BRUCE: We're the same.

1112
01:07:05,300 --> 01:07:09,088
If we're the same, help me.
Train me, let me be your partner.

1113
01:07:11,740 --> 01:07:12,775
No.

1114
01:07:13,220 --> 01:07:14,448
I can't.

1115
01:07:15,220 --> 01:07:17,131
BRUCE: You still have a choice.

1116
01:07:17,860 --> 01:07:19,009
Look, Bruce...

1117
01:07:19,220 --> 01:07:22,018
...I'm a part of this, whether you like it
or not.

1118
01:07:31,500 --> 01:07:33,491
[Lounge music plays, background]

1119
01:07:34,180 --> 01:07:36,171
[Scattered conversations]

1120
01:07:38,940 --> 01:07:42,455
<i>NEWSCASTER: Tonight
all of Gotham society has turned out...</i>

1121
01:07:42,540 --> 01:07:45,896
<i>... for Edward Nygma's gala unveiling
of his New Improved Box.</i>

1122
01:07:47,380 --> 01:07:48,495
Thanks, Al.

1123
01:07:48,660 --> 01:07:49,695
My pleasure, sir.

1124
01:07:49,780 --> 01:07:52,499
<i>NEWSCASTER: They'll be dining
and dancing the night away...</i>

1125
01:07:52,580 --> 01:07:55,253
<i>... on the glamorous roof
of the Ritz Gotham.</i>

1126
01:07:56,340 --> 01:07:59,013
[Upbeat instrumental music, background]

1127
01:08:05,980 --> 01:08:10,053
REPORTER 1: What's it like to have
your face on the cover of every magazine?

1128
01:08:10,420 --> 01:08:14,857
GOSSIP GERTY: How does it feel to be
the city's newest, most-eligible bachelor?

1129
01:08:15,540 --> 01:08:17,178
Gotham must know!

1130
01:08:18,100 --> 01:08:19,852
There's Bruce Wayne!

1131
01:08:20,820 --> 01:08:22,333
GOSSIP GERTY: Brucie!

1132
01:08:23,220 --> 01:08:25,256
SUGAR: Oh, Eddie, he is too cute!

1133
01:08:26,780 --> 01:08:28,975
How come you don't look so good
in that suit?

1134
01:08:29,060 --> 01:08:31,290
Shut up. You're here to work!

1135
01:08:31,980 --> 01:08:33,095
How's my mole?

1136
01:08:33,180 --> 01:08:34,090
Fine.

1137
01:08:34,180 --> 01:08:36,535
REPORTER 2: What about rumors
of a Nygma Tech takeover...

1138
01:08:36,620 --> 01:08:37,609
...of Wayne Enterprises?

1139
01:08:37,700 --> 01:08:41,090
GOSSIP GERTY: Nygma Tech stock is
outselling Wayne Enterprises two to one.

1140
01:08:41,180 --> 01:08:43,296
Are you yesterday's news, Bruce?

1141
01:08:43,380 --> 01:08:44,608
EDWARD: Yes, yes, yes...

1142
01:08:44,700 --> 01:08:46,213
Bruce, old man.

1143
01:08:46,740 --> 01:08:51,416
The press wonders what it's like
to be outsold, outclassed, out-coifed and...

1144
01:08:52,140 --> 01:08:54,210
...generally outdone in every way.

1145
01:08:55,020 --> 01:08:57,011
Hello, Edward. Congratulations.

1146
01:08:57,460 --> 01:08:59,416
Great party. Nice suit.

1147
01:09:00,020 --> 01:09:01,373
Wit. Good.

1148
01:09:02,780 --> 01:09:03,929
EDWARD: And you are?

1149
01:09:04,020 --> 01:09:04,896
Chase.

1150
01:09:06,580 --> 01:09:09,174
And what a grand pursuit you must be.

1151
01:09:12,020 --> 01:09:13,692
I'm Bruce Wayne, Miss...?

1152
01:09:13,780 --> 01:09:14,769
[Giggles]

1153
01:09:15,140 --> 01:09:17,574
You can call me anything you want.

1154
01:09:19,380 --> 01:09:21,257
EDWARD: Ladies and gentlemen...

1155
01:09:21,340 --> 01:09:22,819
...the future!

1156
01:09:23,260 --> 01:09:27,378
My New Improved Box offers
fully-interactive holographic fantasies.

1157
01:09:39,540 --> 01:09:41,531
[Crowd gasps in astonishment]

1158
01:09:46,860 --> 01:09:49,374
Edward, you're dashing and a genius.

1159
01:09:50,460 --> 01:09:52,974
How do you create these images, hon?

1160
01:09:53,500 --> 01:09:55,968
That, my dear, is my little secret.

1161
01:09:58,180 --> 01:10:00,091
[Applause and cheering]

1162
01:10:03,220 --> 01:10:05,097
Fully-interactive holographs.

1163
01:10:05,260 --> 01:10:08,616
BRUCE: Only a high-frequency
carrier wave, beamed into the brain...

1164
01:10:08,700 --> 01:10:10,292
...could create such images.

1165
01:10:10,380 --> 01:10:12,336
And you wish you thought of it.

1166
01:10:12,780 --> 01:10:14,691
EDWARD: Don't be a sore loser.

1167
01:10:14,860 --> 01:10:16,851
Step inside. Give it a try.

1168
01:10:19,180 --> 01:10:22,695
If you can introduce images into the mind,
what stops you from...

1169
01:10:22,860 --> 01:10:25,169
...extracting images out of the mind?

1170
01:10:25,260 --> 01:10:26,249
Oh...

1171
01:10:27,020 --> 01:10:29,488
Too timid to try my machine? Just say so.

1172
01:10:32,860 --> 01:10:34,134
Shall we dance?

1173
01:10:37,220 --> 01:10:38,972
[Waltz melody plays]

1174
01:10:54,460 --> 01:10:56,098
SUGAR: Naughty, naughty.

1175
01:10:56,940 --> 01:10:58,453
Looking for something?

1176
01:10:58,620 --> 01:11:01,373
I was just wondering how you turn it off.

1177
01:11:04,860 --> 01:11:05,895
Clever.

1178
01:11:06,860 --> 01:11:07,815
Thanks.

1179
01:11:07,980 --> 01:11:09,254
My pleasure.

1180
01:11:22,580 --> 01:11:24,571
[Scattered conversations]

1181
01:11:29,660 --> 01:11:30,809
[Ding]

1182
01:11:35,180 --> 01:11:36,169
[Zap]

1183
01:11:37,180 --> 01:11:39,250
<i>COMPUTER: Good evening, Mr. Wayne.</i>

1184
01:11:40,380 --> 01:11:41,529
<i>Relax.</i>

1185
01:11:41,620 --> 01:11:43,736
[Computer speaks in a slow,
hypnotic voice]

1186
01:11:43,820 --> 01:11:45,333
<i>Tell me your...</i>

1187
01:11:46,140 --> 01:11:47,414
<i>... dreams.</i>

1188
01:11:49,020 --> 01:11:50,294
<i>Tell me...</i>

1189
01:11:50,460 --> 01:11:52,132
<i>... your fantasies.</i>

1190
01:11:53,740 --> 01:11:55,537
<i>Tell me your secrets.</i>

1191
01:11:58,060 --> 01:11:59,334
<i>Tell me...</i>

1192
01:12:00,460 --> 01:12:02,132
<i>... your deepest...</i>

1193
01:12:02,460 --> 01:12:03,654
<i>... darkest...</i>

1194
01:12:03,980 --> 01:12:05,254
<i>... fears.</i>

1195
01:12:14,420 --> 01:12:16,058
[Chaotic yelling]

1196
01:12:17,980 --> 01:12:19,299
[Gunshots]

1197
01:12:19,900 --> 01:12:21,219
[Smashing]

1198
01:12:21,740 --> 01:12:23,093
No, no, no!

1199
01:12:26,820 --> 01:12:28,173
[Screaming]

1200
01:12:30,460 --> 01:12:31,734
[Cackles]

1201
01:12:34,700 --> 01:12:36,133
TWO-FACE: Relax, folks!

1202
01:12:36,220 --> 01:12:39,178
<i>It's only an old-fashioned, low-tech stickup!</i>

1203
01:12:39,500 --> 01:12:41,411
<i>We're interested in the basics:</i>

1204
01:12:41,540 --> 01:12:43,610
Cash, jewelry, cellular telephones.

1205
01:12:43,700 --> 01:12:44,849
[Chaotic screaming]

1206
01:12:44,940 --> 01:12:48,455
Hand them over nice and quietly,
and no one will be hurt!

1207
01:12:53,260 --> 01:12:54,932
Emergency, Alfred.

1208
01:12:55,660 --> 01:12:57,013
ALFRED: Yes, sir.

1209
01:12:58,820 --> 01:13:00,538
EDWARD: Be calm, everybody!

1210
01:13:00,620 --> 01:13:01,973
Just stay calm!

1211
01:13:02,140 --> 01:13:03,459
Excuse me!

1212
01:13:06,700 --> 01:13:09,168
EDWARD: You're ruining my big party!
Are you insane?

1213
01:13:09,260 --> 01:13:10,249
[Gulps]

1214
01:13:10,540 --> 01:13:12,929
We're sick of waiting for you
to deliver Batman.

1215
01:13:13,020 --> 01:13:15,011
Patience, O Bifurcated One.

1216
01:13:15,140 --> 01:13:17,176
[Yells] Patience, hell! We want him dead!

1217
01:13:17,260 --> 01:13:20,411
And nothing brings out the Batman
like a little murder and mayhem!

1218
01:13:20,500 --> 01:13:21,296
[Giggles]

1219
01:13:21,380 --> 01:13:23,416
You could have let me in on the caper.

1220
01:13:23,500 --> 01:13:27,095
We could have organized it, planned it,
pre-sold the movie rights!

1221
01:13:27,180 --> 01:13:28,215
Ha!

1222
01:13:29,260 --> 01:13:30,454
[Crash]

1223
01:13:31,540 --> 01:13:32,734
Batman!

1224
01:13:40,540 --> 01:13:42,849
Your entrance was good, his was better.

1225
01:13:45,940 --> 01:13:47,851
[Grunting and groaning]

1226
01:13:50,860 --> 01:13:52,054
The difference?

1227
01:13:52,140 --> 01:13:53,539
Showmanship!

1228
01:13:53,620 --> 01:13:55,258
[Grunting and groaning]

1229
01:13:56,500 --> 01:13:58,138
[Chaotic yelling]

1230
01:14:00,780 --> 01:14:02,179
DICK: Emergency, Alfred.

1231
01:14:02,260 --> 01:14:03,693
ALFRED: Oh, sir...

1232
01:14:04,060 --> 01:14:05,971
I could be fired for this.

1233
01:14:06,980 --> 01:14:09,778
Perhaps they'll have me back
at Buckingham Palace.

1234
01:14:09,860 --> 01:14:13,296
[Chaotic yelling and screaming,
grunting and groaning]

1235
01:14:21,180 --> 01:14:23,330
All right, boys! Phase Two!

1236
01:14:27,420 --> 01:14:29,138
My place, midnight.

1237
01:14:34,220 --> 01:14:35,494
[Cackles]

1238
01:14:40,180 --> 01:14:41,454
[Cackles]

1239
01:14:49,820 --> 01:14:50,889
[Gunshots]

1240
01:14:51,980 --> 01:14:53,618
[Hoots and hollers]

1241
01:14:56,460 --> 01:14:59,258
[Dramatic instrumental music, background]

1242
01:15:09,180 --> 01:15:10,852
[Two-Face cackles]

1243
01:15:20,940 --> 01:15:22,612
[Two-Face cackles]

1244
01:15:32,420 --> 01:15:33,489
[Hissing]

1245
01:15:38,420 --> 01:15:40,490
Nothing like a bad case of gas!

1246
01:15:41,340 --> 01:15:42,568
[Gunshot]

1247
01:15:47,740 --> 01:15:49,332
[Flames roaring]

1248
01:15:54,420 --> 01:15:56,138
[Two-Face cackling]

1249
01:15:57,340 --> 01:15:58,978
[Hooting and hollering]

1250
01:16:01,660 --> 01:16:04,458
[Dramatic instrumental music, background]

1251
01:16:12,020 --> 01:16:14,090
[Shrieks] Why can't you just die?

1252
01:16:14,380 --> 01:16:16,257
[Repeated machine-gun blasts]

1253
01:16:19,300 --> 01:16:21,097
[Thunderous crashing]

1254
01:16:27,860 --> 01:16:29,134
[Cackles]

1255
01:16:51,420 --> 01:16:54,218
[Dramatic instrumental music, background]

1256
01:17:04,540 --> 01:17:05,575
Hi.

1257
01:17:06,580 --> 01:17:08,491
[Dick breathes heavily]

1258
01:17:12,220 --> 01:17:13,778
What were you doing?

1259
01:17:13,940 --> 01:17:16,613
You got a real gratitude problem,
you know that?

1260
01:17:16,700 --> 01:17:19,168
I need a name. Batboy? Knight Wing?

1261
01:17:19,700 --> 01:17:21,770
What's a good sidekick name?

1262
01:17:21,980 --> 01:17:23,971
"Dick Grayson, college student."

1263
01:17:24,060 --> 01:17:25,209
DICK: Screw you!

1264
01:17:25,300 --> 01:17:27,256
I saved your life. You owe me.

1265
01:17:27,420 --> 01:17:29,570
You're going to get yourself killed.

1266
01:17:29,780 --> 01:17:30,974
I'm your new partner.

1267
01:17:31,060 --> 01:17:32,049
No!

1268
01:17:32,660 --> 01:17:37,017
Whenever you go out at night, I'll be
watching. Where Batman goes, I'll go.

1269
01:17:37,180 --> 01:17:38,977
How will you stop me?

1270
01:17:39,620 --> 01:17:41,099
I can stop you.

1271
01:17:44,180 --> 01:17:45,169
Al...

1272
01:17:45,500 --> 01:17:47,456
Hang this next to the Batsuit...

1273
01:17:47,540 --> 01:17:49,019
...where it belongs.

1274
01:17:53,340 --> 01:17:55,251
BRUCE: You're encouraging him.

1275
01:17:56,380 --> 01:17:59,895
Young men with a mind for revenge
need little encouragement.

1276
01:18:00,180 --> 01:18:01,818
They need guidance.

1277
01:18:03,220 --> 01:18:07,372
ALFRED: You, above all, should know
the consequences of the life you choose.

1278
01:18:14,700 --> 01:18:17,339
Even Chase calls being Batman a curse.

1279
01:18:18,100 --> 01:18:20,898
ALFRED: Perhaps the lady is just
what the doctor ordered.

1280
01:18:20,980 --> 01:18:23,016
<i>She seems lovely and wise.</i>

1281
01:18:23,780 --> 01:18:26,055
BRUCE: I've never been in love before.

1282
01:18:26,660 --> 01:18:27,979
Go to her.

1283
01:18:29,460 --> 01:18:31,052
Tell her how you feel.

1284
01:18:31,260 --> 01:18:33,694
She wants Batman, not Bruce Wayne.

1285
01:18:34,460 --> 01:18:35,734
Let her decide.

1286
01:18:55,820 --> 01:18:58,414
[Soft instrumental music, background]

1287
01:19:25,380 --> 01:19:26,813
[Chase gasps]

1288
01:19:27,580 --> 01:19:28,933
CHASE: I'm sorry.

1289
01:19:30,900 --> 01:19:32,652
I can't believe this.

1290
01:19:33,420 --> 01:19:36,492
I've imagined this moment
since I first saw you.

1291
01:19:36,820 --> 01:19:38,219
Your eyes...

1292
01:19:39,100 --> 01:19:40,533
...your lips...

1293
01:19:41,980 --> 01:19:43,299
...your body.

1294
01:19:45,380 --> 01:19:47,177
CHASE: Now I have you and...

1295
01:19:48,820 --> 01:19:51,380
...I'm wishing you were somebody else.

1296
01:19:53,460 --> 01:19:54,449
[Sighs]

1297
01:19:56,660 --> 01:19:59,220
I guess a girl has to grow up sometime.

1298
01:20:01,260 --> 01:20:02,898
CHASE: I've met someone.

1299
01:20:08,420 --> 01:20:09,739
He's not you.

1300
01:20:12,060 --> 01:20:14,051
I hope you can understand.

1301
01:20:19,180 --> 01:20:20,613
I understand.

1302
01:20:25,500 --> 01:20:26,649
Well...

1303
01:20:35,220 --> 01:20:36,369
[Zoom]

1304
01:20:41,900 --> 01:20:43,492
[Two-Face wails]

1305
01:20:47,900 --> 01:20:49,811
That's just what I said.

1306
01:20:50,540 --> 01:20:53,054
Then I taught my doggie a new trick:

1307
01:20:53,820 --> 01:20:55,731
How to map the human mind.

1308
01:20:55,980 --> 01:20:59,450
Would you like to see
what Bruce Wayne has in his head?

1309
01:21:02,540 --> 01:21:03,529
[Hollers]

1310
01:21:12,740 --> 01:21:14,253
Riddle me this:

1311
01:21:15,100 --> 01:21:16,772
What kind of man...

1312
01:21:16,940 --> 01:21:18,931
...has bats on the brain?

1313
01:21:19,020 --> 01:21:20,851
[Two-Face howls and cackles]

1314
01:21:22,540 --> 01:21:25,100
- Go ahead. You can say it.
- You're a genius.

1315
01:21:25,260 --> 01:21:26,534
Oh, stop.

1316
01:21:26,620 --> 01:21:27,814
[Both giggle]

1317
01:21:30,020 --> 01:21:31,931
BRUCE: So, from this day on...

1318
01:21:32,460 --> 01:21:34,212
...Batman is no more.

1319
01:21:36,460 --> 01:21:38,052
DICK: You can't just quit.

1320
01:21:38,140 --> 01:21:41,337
There's monsters out there.
Batman has to protect the innocent.

1321
01:21:41,420 --> 01:21:45,015
BRUCE: I've dedicated my life to helping
strangers I've never met.

1322
01:21:45,380 --> 01:21:47,211
Faces I've never seen.

1323
01:21:47,580 --> 01:21:48,774
BRUCE: Well...

1324
01:21:49,220 --> 01:21:51,609
...the innocent aren't faceless anymore.

1325
01:21:52,460 --> 01:21:55,258
You can't tell me what to do
with the rest of my life.

1326
01:21:55,340 --> 01:21:58,298
My dad told me that every man goes
his own way.

1327
01:21:58,420 --> 01:22:00,376
DICK: My way goes to Two-Face.

1328
01:22:00,780 --> 01:22:02,372
You must help me.

1329
01:22:02,940 --> 01:22:05,010
BRUCE: And if you do find Harvey...

1330
01:22:05,100 --> 01:22:06,533
...and then you kill him...

1331
01:22:06,620 --> 01:22:07,814
...what next?

1332
01:22:08,340 --> 01:22:09,489
[Dick sighs]

1333
01:22:11,500 --> 01:22:12,728
BRUCE: Exactly.

1334
01:22:13,260 --> 01:22:15,455
Then you'd be alone, like me.

1335
01:22:18,300 --> 01:22:20,291
BRUCE: No, you must let this go.

1336
01:22:20,500 --> 01:22:22,218
Listen to me, I'm your friend.

1337
01:22:22,300 --> 01:22:24,894
DICK: I don't need a friend,
I need a partner.

1338
01:22:25,100 --> 01:22:26,852
Two-Face has got to pay.

1339
01:22:28,300 --> 01:22:29,335
Please.

1340
01:22:31,500 --> 01:22:34,810
Chase is coming for dinner.
I'm going to tell her...

1341
01:22:35,740 --> 01:22:36,934
...everything.

1342
01:22:39,140 --> 01:22:40,937
Come upstairs. We'll talk.

1343
01:22:41,020 --> 01:22:43,773
[Dramatic instrumental beat, background]

1344
01:22:55,460 --> 01:22:57,894
ALFRED: Good evening.
CHASE: Good evening.

1345
01:22:58,220 --> 01:22:59,573
ALFRED: Happy Halloween.

1346
01:22:59,660 --> 01:23:01,571
CHASE: Happy Halloween to you.

1347
01:23:29,660 --> 01:23:31,093
[Rat squeaks]

1348
01:23:34,220 --> 01:23:38,611
I asked you here tonight because
there's something I wanted to tell you.

1349
01:23:39,420 --> 01:23:41,650
I wanted to tell you something too.

1350
01:23:42,100 --> 01:23:43,328
BRUCE: What I wanted...

1351
01:23:43,420 --> 01:23:44,535
[Both laugh]

1352
01:23:44,620 --> 01:23:46,372
BRUCE: Go ahead, you first.

1353
01:23:50,740 --> 01:23:52,253
Trick or treat!

1354
01:23:52,340 --> 01:23:53,409
[Giggling]

1355
01:23:54,140 --> 01:23:56,176
All my life I have been...

1356
01:23:56,940 --> 01:23:59,249
...attracted to a certain kind of man.

1357
01:23:59,380 --> 01:24:00,608
The wrong kind.

1358
01:24:01,100 --> 01:24:03,375
CHASE: Look at what I do for a living.

1359
01:24:06,500 --> 01:24:07,819
And since...

1360
01:24:08,020 --> 01:24:09,976
...since I met you, I...

1361
01:24:12,380 --> 01:24:13,608
Oh, God.

1362
01:24:14,060 --> 01:24:15,618
Why am I so nervous?

1363
01:24:15,700 --> 01:24:16,496
[Clanking]

1364
01:24:16,580 --> 01:24:17,979
CHASE: [Gasps] Oh!

1365
01:24:21,020 --> 01:24:22,339
[Gunshot echoes]

1366
01:24:23,380 --> 01:24:27,009
Don't eat too much tonight
or you'll be sick in your beds.

1367
01:24:33,100 --> 01:24:35,489
[Upbeat instrumental music, background]

1368
01:24:44,060 --> 01:24:46,210
[Children giggle and talk excitedly]

1369
01:24:54,060 --> 01:24:55,459
[Two-Face cackles]

1370
01:24:57,180 --> 01:24:58,772
Happy Halloween!

1371
01:25:03,860 --> 01:25:05,498
[Thunder rumbles]

1372
01:25:12,220 --> 01:25:13,573
What's wrong?

1373
01:25:14,660 --> 01:25:16,013
BRUCE: It's happening again.

1374
01:25:16,100 --> 01:25:17,328
Flashes.

1375
01:25:18,020 --> 01:25:19,578
My parents' death.

1376
01:25:20,700 --> 01:25:23,089
Your memories are trying
to break through.

1377
01:25:23,180 --> 01:25:25,091
BRUCE: I want to tell you something.

1378
01:25:25,180 --> 01:25:27,011
Something I've never told anyone.

1379
01:25:27,100 --> 01:25:28,453
CHASE: It's all right.

1380
01:25:28,540 --> 01:25:30,258
It's all right. I'm here.

1381
01:25:36,260 --> 01:25:38,216
<i>CHASE: [Voice echoing] I'm here.</i>

1382
01:25:40,180 --> 01:25:41,818
[Priest reciting prayers]

1383
01:25:41,900 --> 01:25:44,209
<i>BRUCE: The night of my parents' wake...</i>

1384
01:25:44,620 --> 01:25:47,009
<i>... the priest's words gave no comfort.</i>

1385
01:25:48,740 --> 01:25:50,059
<i>Of course.</i>

1386
01:25:51,340 --> 01:25:53,331
<i>There, on my father's desk...</i>

1387
01:25:53,500 --> 01:25:55,092
<i>... the red book.</i>

1388
01:25:55,340 --> 01:25:56,739
<i>His journal.</i>

1389
01:25:57,100 --> 01:25:59,091
<i>He'd written in it every day.</i>

1390
01:25:59,900 --> 01:26:02,175
<i>But now he'd never write in it again.</i>

1391
01:26:03,340 --> 01:26:04,773
<i>At that moment I knew...</i>

1392
01:26:04,860 --> 01:26:06,930
<i>... my life would never be the same.</i>

1393
01:26:13,500 --> 01:26:15,695
<i>I raced out into the storm...</i>

1394
01:26:16,300 --> 01:26:18,211
<i>... trying to outrun the rage.</i>

1395
01:26:18,380 --> 01:26:19,495
<i>The pain.</i>

1396
01:26:20,420 --> 01:26:21,819
<i>Then I fell.</i>

1397
01:26:23,660 --> 01:26:25,173
<i>I fell forever.</i>

1398
01:26:27,140 --> 01:26:29,051
<i>The cave was monstrous.</i>

1399
01:26:30,300 --> 01:26:32,575
<i>It must have been there for centuries.</i>

1400
01:26:34,620 --> 01:26:35,769
<i>And there...</i>

1401
01:26:36,540 --> 01:26:38,212
<i>... deep in the shadows...</i>

1402
01:26:39,620 --> 01:26:40,848
<i>... I saw...</i>

1403
01:26:43,180 --> 01:26:45,136
<i>It was coming toward me.</i>

1404
01:26:45,900 --> 01:26:48,619
<i>I was scared at first, but only at first.</i>

1405
01:26:50,140 --> 01:26:52,700
<i>The figure in the dark was my destiny.</i>

1406
01:26:53,900 --> 01:26:56,016
<i>It would change my life forever.</i>

1407
01:26:58,140 --> 01:27:02,531
<i>I would use its image to strike terror
into the hearts of those who did evil.</i>

1408
01:27:02,660 --> 01:27:06,892
<i>I would ensure what happened to me
would never happen to anyone else.</i>

1409
01:27:07,980 --> 01:27:09,732
<i>I would have my revenge.</i>

1410
01:27:13,420 --> 01:27:15,695
CHASE: What are you trying to tell me?

1411
01:27:17,900 --> 01:27:19,094
BRUCE: I'm...

1412
01:27:52,380 --> 01:27:53,893
Twick or tweet!

1413
01:27:56,980 --> 01:27:57,969
[Bang]

1414
01:27:58,860 --> 01:27:59,929
[Crash]

1415
01:28:00,780 --> 01:28:01,929
Trick.

1416
01:28:08,780 --> 01:28:10,293
[Whispers] Remember the plan?

1417
01:28:10,380 --> 01:28:12,052
Seize and capture.

1418
01:28:12,740 --> 01:28:13,809
No killing.

1419
01:28:13,900 --> 01:28:15,891
That goes double for you.

1420
01:28:15,980 --> 01:28:17,208
[Thugs chuckle]

1421
01:28:18,500 --> 01:28:20,491
RIDDLER: If I was a superhero...

1422
01:28:21,260 --> 01:28:23,091
...where would I hide?

1423
01:28:27,860 --> 01:28:29,339
[Whispers] Spank me.

1424
01:28:31,380 --> 01:28:34,850
[Chaotic yelling,
dramatic instrumental beat, background]

1425
01:28:41,620 --> 01:28:44,180
<i>LOUDSPEAKER:
Intruder alert! Intruder alert!</i>

1426
01:28:46,900 --> 01:28:49,050
RIDDLER: Intruder alert! Intruder alert!

1427
01:28:49,140 --> 01:28:50,459
[Yells] Shut up!

1428
01:29:00,660 --> 01:29:02,571
Now, that's impressive!

1429
01:29:04,540 --> 01:29:05,529
[Ding]

1430
01:29:06,340 --> 01:29:07,853
[Chase screams]

1431
01:29:16,420 --> 01:29:17,933
[Fast-paced instrumental music,
background]

1432
01:29:18,020 --> 01:29:21,456
It's always risky introducing
a tamed animal into the wild.

1433
01:29:25,540 --> 01:29:26,609
[Ticking]

1434
01:29:26,700 --> 01:29:27,689
[Bounce]

1435
01:29:28,220 --> 01:29:29,335
[Explosion]

1436
01:29:31,700 --> 01:29:33,736
[Riddler hums and giggles]

1437
01:29:35,180 --> 01:29:38,695
They may have trouble adapting
to their new environment.

1438
01:29:41,780 --> 01:29:42,974
[Bounce]

1439
01:29:43,980 --> 01:29:45,095
[Explosion]

1440
01:29:48,740 --> 01:29:49,968
[Groaning and yelling]

1441
01:29:50,060 --> 01:29:51,049
[Sighs]

1442
01:29:53,340 --> 01:29:54,455
[Snickering]

1443
01:29:56,380 --> 01:29:57,733
[Explosion]

1444
01:30:00,740 --> 01:30:03,379
[Electronic organ rhythm
as in a baseball game]

1445
01:30:05,060 --> 01:30:06,413
[Explosion]

1446
01:30:06,620 --> 01:30:08,019
[Grunts] Yeah!

1447
01:30:08,980 --> 01:30:10,129
[Ding]

1448
01:30:13,140 --> 01:30:14,778
[Groaning and shouting]

1449
01:30:15,220 --> 01:30:17,290
Somebody tell the fat lady...

1450
01:30:17,460 --> 01:30:19,178
...she's on in five.

1451
01:30:19,260 --> 01:30:21,091
[Electronic squeaking]

1452
01:30:22,820 --> 01:30:24,458
[Riddler giggles]

1453
01:30:26,380 --> 01:30:27,495
[Explosion]

1454
01:30:33,260 --> 01:30:35,057
[Laughs hysterically]

1455
01:30:36,740 --> 01:30:38,173
[Shouts] "Joygasm!"

1456
01:30:41,060 --> 01:30:42,413
[Chaotic yelling]

1457
01:30:50,940 --> 01:30:52,009
[Cackles]

1458
01:30:54,220 --> 01:30:55,494
[Gunshot]

1459
01:30:55,780 --> 01:30:57,293
[Chase screams]

1460
01:30:59,940 --> 01:31:01,578
TWO-FACE: Get the girl!

1461
01:31:10,140 --> 01:31:11,368
[Shrieks] No!

1462
01:31:12,300 --> 01:31:13,813
Don't kill him.

1463
01:31:15,700 --> 01:31:17,258
If you kill him...

1464
01:31:25,740 --> 01:31:27,458
...he won't learn nothing.

1465
01:31:27,540 --> 01:31:28,939
[Two-Face cackles]

1466
01:31:30,020 --> 01:31:31,373
[Riddler cackles]

1467
01:31:32,380 --> 01:31:33,813
[Running footsteps]

1468
01:31:36,700 --> 01:31:38,213
[Chase screams]

1469
01:31:48,260 --> 01:31:51,058
[Dramatic instrumental music, background]

1470
01:32:01,420 --> 01:32:03,650
ALFRED: [Voice echoing] Master Bruce!

1471
01:32:10,380 --> 01:32:12,132
How are you, young man?

1472
01:32:13,460 --> 01:32:16,293
You haven't called me that for a long time.

1473
01:32:16,580 --> 01:32:18,332
Old habits die hard.

1474
01:32:19,180 --> 01:32:20,579
Are you all right?

1475
01:32:21,300 --> 01:32:22,528
Where's Chase?

1476
01:32:22,700 --> 01:32:24,930
ALFRED: I'm afraid they've taken her.

1477
01:32:25,100 --> 01:32:27,056
Master Dick has run away.

1478
01:32:27,700 --> 01:32:29,531
The cave has been destroyed.

1479
01:32:30,460 --> 01:32:32,576
ALFRED: And there's another riddle.

1480
01:32:33,540 --> 01:32:35,815
[Loud, distorted sound effects]

1481
01:32:39,140 --> 01:32:40,619
[Chase groans]

1482
01:32:42,940 --> 01:32:44,851
RIDDLER: I'm coming, my sweet.

1483
01:32:49,100 --> 01:32:50,658
RIDDLER: Like the jacket?

1484
01:32:50,740 --> 01:32:52,651
It keeps me safe when I'm...

1485
01:32:52,820 --> 01:32:54,538
...jogging at night.

1486
01:32:55,420 --> 01:32:57,058
Batman will come for me.

1487
01:32:58,300 --> 01:32:59,494
Batman?

1488
01:33:00,620 --> 01:33:02,895
[With British accent] Batman, you say?

1489
01:33:03,380 --> 01:33:04,893
Coming for you?

1490
01:33:05,180 --> 01:33:06,454
[Hollers]

1491
01:33:08,180 --> 01:33:09,329
I'm...

1492
01:33:09,940 --> 01:33:11,771
[Shrieks]... counting on it.

1493
01:33:16,140 --> 01:33:19,018
COMMISSIONER: What is that?
Where's it coming from?

1494
01:33:19,860 --> 01:33:20,770
There!

1495
01:33:21,100 --> 01:33:22,818
OFFICER: Who's doing that?

1496
01:33:23,260 --> 01:33:24,818
COMMISSIONER: The Riddler!

1497
01:33:25,540 --> 01:33:28,498
BRUCE: "We're five little items
of an everyday sort.

1498
01:33:30,100 --> 01:33:32,568
<i>"You'll find us all in a tennis court."</i>

1499
01:33:33,060 --> 01:33:34,254
BRUCE: In...

1500
01:33:34,340 --> 01:33:35,659
A-E-l-O-U.

1501
01:33:36,820 --> 01:33:37,775
Vowels.

1502
01:33:37,940 --> 01:33:39,532
Not entirely unclever, sir.

1503
01:33:39,620 --> 01:33:42,259
But what do a clock, a match,
chess pawns...

1504
01:33:42,340 --> 01:33:45,616
...and vowels have in common?
What do these riddles mean?

1505
01:33:45,780 --> 01:33:49,056
BRUCE: Every riddle contains a number
and they arrived in this order:

1506
01:33:49,140 --> 01:33:50,493
<i>13, 1, 8...</i>

1507
01:33:51,460 --> 01:33:52,336
<i>... and 5.</i>

1508
01:33:52,420 --> 01:33:54,058
ALFRED: 13, 1, 8 and 5.

1509
01:33:55,220 --> 01:33:56,175
<i>Meaning?</i>

1510
01:33:56,340 --> 01:33:58,171
BRUCE: Letters of the alphabet?

1511
01:33:58,260 --> 01:33:59,978
Of course, 13 is M.

1512
01:34:00,260 --> 01:34:03,138
BRUCE: 1 would be A, 8 would be H
and 5 would be E.

1513
01:34:03,780 --> 01:34:05,099
ALFRED: M-A-H-E.

1514
01:34:06,500 --> 01:34:08,411
BRUCE: Perhaps 1 and 8 are 18.

1515
01:34:09,700 --> 01:34:10,928
18 is R.

1516
01:34:12,100 --> 01:34:13,169
M-R-E.

1517
01:34:15,620 --> 01:34:16,735
How about...

1518
01:34:16,820 --> 01:34:18,173
..."Mr. E"?

1519
01:34:18,420 --> 01:34:20,490
ALFRED: Mystery?
BRUCE: Another name for mystery?

1520
01:34:20,580 --> 01:34:21,535
Enigma.

1521
01:34:22,020 --> 01:34:23,453
Mr. E. Nygma.

1522
01:34:24,180 --> 01:34:25,454
Edward Nygma.

1523
01:34:25,860 --> 01:34:29,694
BRUCE: Stickley's suicide was obviously
a computer-generated forgery.

1524
01:34:29,820 --> 01:34:33,176
ALFRED: You really are quite bright,
despite what people say.

1525
01:34:33,860 --> 01:34:35,930
BRUCE: Are all the Batsuits destroyed?

1526
01:34:36,020 --> 01:34:40,616
All except the prototype with the sonar
modifications. But it's not tested.

1527
01:34:41,460 --> 01:34:43,098
Tonight's a good night.

1528
01:34:46,180 --> 01:34:47,898
[Metallic clanking]

1529
01:34:54,380 --> 01:34:56,655
BATMAN: What do you suggest? By sea...

1530
01:34:58,420 --> 01:34:59,853
<i>... or by air?</i>

1531
01:35:04,620 --> 01:35:06,099
ROBIN: Why not both?

1532
01:35:14,420 --> 01:35:15,773
Who's your tailor?

1533
01:35:15,860 --> 01:35:17,816
I took the liberty, sir.

1534
01:35:20,580 --> 01:35:21,729
BATMAN: "R?"

1535
01:35:21,860 --> 01:35:23,452
What's that stand for?

1536
01:35:25,300 --> 01:35:26,255
Robin.

1537
01:35:27,660 --> 01:35:30,413
Riddler and Two-Face can make
a pretty lethal combination.

1538
01:35:30,500 --> 01:35:32,013
You could use a hand.

1539
01:35:32,260 --> 01:35:34,251
Two against two are better odds.

1540
01:35:34,820 --> 01:35:37,050
I can't promise I won't kill Harvey.

1541
01:35:37,660 --> 01:35:39,855
"A man's got to go his own way."

1542
01:35:40,140 --> 01:35:41,778
A friend taught me that.

1543
01:35:42,580 --> 01:35:44,093
Not just a friend.

1544
01:35:46,500 --> 01:35:47,819
A partner.

1545
01:35:49,700 --> 01:35:51,258
[Batmobile engine roars]

1546
01:36:02,980 --> 01:36:04,208
[Robin hollers]

1547
01:36:19,700 --> 01:36:21,611
COMMISSIONER: He's not coming.

1548
01:36:21,860 --> 01:36:23,293
Shut it down.

1549
01:36:33,140 --> 01:36:35,370
Wait a minute! Wait a minute!

1550
01:36:35,460 --> 01:36:37,098
[Batmobile engine roars]

1551
01:36:41,220 --> 01:36:42,539
[Yells] Hey, go!

1552
01:36:46,700 --> 01:36:47,928
Go! Go!

1553
01:36:52,620 --> 01:36:55,054
[Dramatic instrumental music, background]

1554
01:37:05,180 --> 01:37:06,932
[Electronic beeping]

1555
01:37:09,260 --> 01:37:11,251
[Two-Face and Riddler giggle]

1556
01:37:12,700 --> 01:37:13,610
A-14.

1557
01:37:13,700 --> 01:37:15,053
[Explosion]

1558
01:37:17,980 --> 01:37:18,969
[Beeping]

1559
01:37:19,300 --> 01:37:20,016
Hit!

1560
01:37:20,100 --> 01:37:21,010
Sweet!

1561
01:37:21,820 --> 01:37:23,048
TWO-FACE: B-12.

1562
01:37:24,220 --> 01:37:25,573
[Explosion]

1563
01:37:26,580 --> 01:37:27,569
RIDDLER: Hit!

1564
01:37:27,660 --> 01:37:28,934
My favorite vitamin.

1565
01:37:29,020 --> 01:37:30,533
TWO-FACE: Ha, ha, ha!

1566
01:37:30,780 --> 01:37:32,259
[Electronic hissing]

1567
01:37:32,340 --> 01:37:33,489
[Laughs] Oh!

1568
01:37:36,220 --> 01:37:37,255
[Zooming]

1569
01:37:39,100 --> 01:37:40,897
That sinking feeling.

1570
01:37:41,100 --> 01:37:42,374
I like this game.

1571
01:37:42,460 --> 01:37:43,654
TWO-FACE: C-9.

1572
01:37:43,980 --> 01:37:45,333
[Explosion]

1573
01:37:48,020 --> 01:37:49,578
[Thunderous explosion]

1574
01:37:52,220 --> 01:37:53,448
[Riddler gasps]

1575
01:37:54,020 --> 01:37:55,931
You sunk my battleship!

1576
01:37:56,740 --> 01:37:57,968
Who, me?

1577
01:37:58,140 --> 01:37:59,493
[Riddler cackles]

1578
01:38:01,620 --> 01:38:02,894
[Beeping]

1579
01:38:16,980 --> 01:38:18,254
[Beeping]

1580
01:38:21,620 --> 01:38:23,178
This is your captain speaking.

1581
01:38:23,260 --> 01:38:27,173
Please return to your seats.
We will be experiencing turbulence.

1582
01:38:28,620 --> 01:38:29,609
[Zap]

1583
01:38:30,300 --> 01:38:31,653
[Explosion]

1584
01:38:32,420 --> 01:38:33,409
[Shrieks]

1585
01:38:34,660 --> 01:38:35,979
I got him!

1586
01:38:42,540 --> 01:38:45,134
I hope they can find the little black box.

1587
01:38:49,180 --> 01:38:50,533
[Explosion]

1588
01:38:53,300 --> 01:38:55,734
[Dramatic instrumental music, background]

1589
01:39:16,860 --> 01:39:18,134
[Gasping]

1590
01:39:28,420 --> 01:39:29,569
Now...

1591
01:39:31,500 --> 01:39:33,456
...the real game begins.

1592
01:39:40,900 --> 01:39:43,494
ROBIN: Holy rusted metal, Batman!
BATMAN: Huh?

1593
01:39:44,580 --> 01:39:46,252
ROBIN: The ground, it's all metal.

1594
01:39:46,340 --> 01:39:48,331
It's full of holes: holey.

1595
01:39:50,780 --> 01:39:52,736
[Loud, distorted sound effects]

1596
01:39:53,460 --> 01:39:54,654
BATMAN: Wait!

1597
01:39:56,740 --> 01:39:58,810
ROBIN: The whole island's moving!

1598
01:40:42,900 --> 01:40:44,413
Looking for us?

1599
01:40:46,940 --> 01:40:48,851
[Grunting and groaning]

1600
01:40:49,060 --> 01:40:50,971
ROBIN: That was for my mother!

1601
01:40:51,100 --> 01:40:52,169
My father!

1602
01:40:54,940 --> 01:40:56,089
My brother!

1603
01:40:57,220 --> 01:40:58,778
And this is for me!

1604
01:41:00,340 --> 01:41:02,012
[Short, panicked screams]

1605
01:41:10,420 --> 01:41:13,218
[Dramatic instrumental music, background]

1606
01:41:19,340 --> 01:41:21,615
[Loud, distorted sound effects]

1607
01:41:29,100 --> 01:41:31,330
TWO-FACE: Finally, justice is served!

1608
01:41:32,620 --> 01:41:33,973
Let us die!

1609
01:41:42,420 --> 01:41:45,139
TWO-FACE: You're a man
after our own heart, son!

1610
01:41:45,220 --> 01:41:47,097
[Gasps] I'll see you in hell!

1611
01:41:51,380 --> 01:41:52,733
[Both gasping]

1612
01:41:52,900 --> 01:41:54,652
I'd rather see you in jail!

1613
01:41:55,140 --> 01:41:56,414
[Gasping]

1614
01:41:58,820 --> 01:42:00,890
TWO-FACE: Oh, good boy. Good boy.

1615
01:42:01,380 --> 01:42:03,018
The Bat's taught you well.

1616
01:42:03,100 --> 01:42:04,215
TWO-FACE: Noble.

1617
01:42:04,300 --> 01:42:05,574
Stupid...

1618
01:42:06,180 --> 01:42:07,499
...but noble.

1619
01:42:10,980 --> 01:42:13,255
[Loud, distorted sound effects]

1620
01:42:17,780 --> 01:42:19,179
[Screeching]

1621
01:42:50,220 --> 01:42:51,733
Riddle me this.

1622
01:42:52,260 --> 01:42:53,773
Riddle me that.

1623
01:42:54,060 --> 01:42:56,494
Who's afraid of the big black bat?

1624
01:42:57,580 --> 01:42:59,218
No more tricks, Edward.

1625
01:42:59,620 --> 01:43:01,133
Very well, then.

1626
01:43:05,700 --> 01:43:07,179
Let's get real.

1627
01:43:07,620 --> 01:43:09,929
Release Chase.
This is between you and me.

1628
01:43:10,020 --> 01:43:11,055
And me...

1629
01:43:11,180 --> 01:43:12,579
[Yells]... and me!

1630
01:43:13,180 --> 01:43:14,533
[Riddler cackles]

1631
01:43:15,460 --> 01:43:20,090
You've sucked Gotham's brain waves and
now you've devised a way to read minds.

1632
01:43:20,180 --> 01:43:21,579
[Riddler cackles]

1633
01:43:22,260 --> 01:43:23,659
RIDDLER: You betcha!

1634
01:43:23,740 --> 01:43:27,699
Soon my little Box will be
on countless TV's around the world...

1635
01:43:28,420 --> 01:43:30,888
...feeding me credit-card numbers...

1636
01:43:31,020 --> 01:43:32,692
RIDDLER: bank codes...

1637
01:43:32,820 --> 01:43:34,538
...sexual fantasies...

1638
01:43:34,740 --> 01:43:36,731
...and little white lies.

1639
01:43:37,380 --> 01:43:39,336
Into my head they'll go.

1640
01:43:39,660 --> 01:43:42,094
RIDDLER: [Giggles] Victory is inevitable.

1641
01:43:42,340 --> 01:43:44,331
For if knowledge is power...

1642
01:43:45,380 --> 01:43:46,972
...then a god...

1643
01:43:47,140 --> 01:43:48,095
...am...

1644
01:43:49,140 --> 01:43:50,209
[Growls]... I!

1645
01:43:50,300 --> 01:43:51,779
[Continues growling]

1646
01:43:56,580 --> 01:43:59,253
Was that over the top? I can never tell.

1647
01:43:59,340 --> 01:44:00,455
[Cackles]

1648
01:44:02,500 --> 01:44:05,219
By the way, I've seen your mind. Freak!

1649
01:44:05,980 --> 01:44:08,050
Yours is the greatest riddle of all!

1650
01:44:08,140 --> 01:44:11,132
RIDDLER: Can Bruce Wayne and Batman
ever truly coexist?

1651
01:44:12,260 --> 01:44:13,852
We'll find out today!

1652
01:44:15,060 --> 01:44:17,699
But first, let's meet our contestants.

1653
01:44:18,700 --> 01:44:20,418
RIDDLER: Behind curtain...

1654
01:44:21,220 --> 01:44:22,812
...number one...

1655
01:44:25,900 --> 01:44:28,892
RIDDLER: the absolutely fabulous
Dr. Chase Meridian!

1656
01:44:28,980 --> 01:44:30,095
[Chase groans]

1657
01:44:30,180 --> 01:44:31,932
She enjoys hiking, manicures...

1658
01:44:32,020 --> 01:44:35,456
RIDDLER: and foolishly hopes
to be the love of Bruce's life.

1659
01:44:36,420 --> 01:44:37,933
[Squeals and cackles]

1660
01:44:38,420 --> 01:44:39,409
Ha!

1661
01:44:40,980 --> 01:44:42,811
Behind curtain number two...

1662
01:44:45,900 --> 01:44:48,130
..."Fatman's" one and only partner.

1663
01:44:48,580 --> 01:44:50,491
RIDDLER: This acrobat turned orphan...

1664
01:44:50,580 --> 01:44:54,095
...likes Saturday-morning cartoons
and dreams of one day being...

1665
01:44:54,220 --> 01:44:56,256
...bare-naked with a girl.

1666
01:44:56,340 --> 01:44:57,329
Ha!

1667
01:44:57,420 --> 01:44:58,773
[Riddler cackles]

1668
01:44:59,780 --> 01:45:01,896
And below these contestants...

1669
01:45:02,100 --> 01:45:04,011
...my personal favorite:

1670
01:45:04,260 --> 01:45:05,898
RIDDLER: A watery grave.

1671
01:45:08,300 --> 01:45:09,938
Just one little touch...

1672
01:45:10,340 --> 01:45:13,537
RIDDLER: and five seconds later
these two players are...

1673
01:45:13,620 --> 01:45:15,611
...gull feed on the rocks below.

1674
01:45:15,700 --> 01:45:16,689
Ha!

1675
01:45:18,420 --> 01:45:20,490
Not enough time to save them both.

1676
01:45:20,660 --> 01:45:21,775
Oooh!

1677
01:45:24,300 --> 01:45:26,495
Which one will it be, Batman?

1678
01:45:26,660 --> 01:45:28,173
RIDDLER: Bruce's love?

1679
01:45:28,260 --> 01:45:30,774
<i>Or the Dark Knight's junior partner?</i>

1680
01:45:30,860 --> 01:45:32,578
[Simulated ticking]

1681
01:45:33,580 --> 01:45:36,572
BATMAN: There is no way for me
to save them or myself.

1682
01:45:37,180 --> 01:45:39,410
It's all one giant death-trap.

1683
01:45:39,620 --> 01:45:40,530
Judges?

1684
01:45:40,620 --> 01:45:41,609
[Honks]

1685
01:45:42,180 --> 01:45:44,819
<i>I'm sorry. Your answer must be
in the form of a question.</i>

1686
01:45:44,900 --> 01:45:46,572
But thank you for playing.

1687
01:45:46,660 --> 01:45:47,854
BATMAN: Wait!

1688
01:45:48,940 --> 01:45:50,293
I have a riddle for you.

1689
01:45:50,380 --> 01:45:51,495
For me?

1690
01:45:53,260 --> 01:45:54,659
[Whispers] Really?

1691
01:45:57,540 --> 01:45:58,768
Tell me.

1692
01:46:02,340 --> 01:46:03,853
I see without seeing.

1693
01:46:04,620 --> 01:46:07,373
To me, darkness is as clear as daylight.

1694
01:46:09,060 --> 01:46:10,129
What am I?

1695
01:46:11,500 --> 01:46:12,819
RIDDLER: Please!

1696
01:46:13,380 --> 01:46:15,371
You're as blind as a bat!

1697
01:46:16,140 --> 01:46:17,129
Exactly.

1698
01:46:17,220 --> 01:46:18,414
[Click]

1699
01:46:20,780 --> 01:46:22,008
[Swoosh]

1700
01:46:22,540 --> 01:46:23,734
[Sugar screams]

1701
01:46:23,820 --> 01:46:25,173
[Explosion]

1702
01:46:33,260 --> 01:46:35,091
[Thunderous explosion]

1703
01:46:42,820 --> 01:46:44,333
[Riddler moans]

1704
01:46:52,780 --> 01:46:53,974
Bummer!

1705
01:46:57,060 --> 01:46:59,335
[Loud, distorted sound effects]

1706
01:47:09,020 --> 01:47:10,248
[Chase screams]

1707
01:47:20,700 --> 01:47:21,974
[Zooming]

1708
01:47:46,260 --> 01:47:49,058
[Dramatic instrumental music, background]

1709
01:47:55,860 --> 01:47:57,088
[Gasps] Thanks.

1710
01:48:08,980 --> 01:48:10,254
[Cackles]

1711
01:48:10,460 --> 01:48:12,291
All those heroics for nothing.

1712
01:48:12,380 --> 01:48:15,053
No more riddles,
no more curtains one and two.

1713
01:48:15,260 --> 01:48:16,978
TWO-FACE: Just plain curtains!

1714
01:48:17,060 --> 01:48:18,049
[Cackles]

1715
01:48:18,940 --> 01:48:20,931
Aren't you forgetting something?

1716
01:48:21,100 --> 01:48:22,215
Your coin.

1717
01:48:24,060 --> 01:48:25,812
You're always of two minds.

1718
01:48:27,140 --> 01:48:29,051
Yes, of course. You're right.

1719
01:48:29,660 --> 01:48:32,128
Emotion's always the enemy
of true justice.

1720
01:48:32,220 --> 01:48:34,290
You've always been a good friend.

1721
01:48:37,940 --> 01:48:39,851
[Short, panicked gasps]

1722
01:48:41,500 --> 01:48:42,774
[Screaming]

1723
01:48:59,060 --> 01:49:01,858
[Dramatic instrumental music, background]

1724
01:49:19,100 --> 01:49:20,169
[Sobs] Why?

1725
01:49:21,300 --> 01:49:22,619
Why can't I...

1726
01:49:22,740 --> 01:49:24,253
RIDDLER: kill you?

1727
01:49:27,500 --> 01:49:29,218
Too many questions.

1728
01:49:29,740 --> 01:49:31,253
Too many questions.

1729
01:49:32,060 --> 01:49:33,288
Poor Edward.

1730
01:49:33,980 --> 01:49:35,891
I had to save them both.

1731
01:49:36,380 --> 01:49:39,019
You see, I'm both Bruce Wayne
and Batman.

1732
01:49:39,740 --> 01:49:41,571
Not because I have to be.

1733
01:49:41,740 --> 01:49:42,855
Now...

1734
01:49:43,380 --> 01:49:45,291
...because I choose to be.

1735
01:49:50,380 --> 01:49:51,654
[Wailing]

1736
01:50:07,620 --> 01:50:09,850
DR. BURTON:
Thanks for responding to my request...

1737
01:50:09,940 --> 01:50:12,090
<i>... for a consultation, Dr. Meridian.</i>

1738
01:50:12,260 --> 01:50:13,454
Edward Nygma...

1739
01:50:13,620 --> 01:50:17,295
...has been screaming for hours
that he knows the true identity...

1740
01:50:17,460 --> 01:50:18,893
...of Batman.

1741
01:50:32,100 --> 01:50:33,294
CHASE: Edward?

1742
01:50:34,020 --> 01:50:35,214
EDWARD: Who...

1743
01:50:35,660 --> 01:50:36,934
<i>... is it?</i>

1744
01:50:39,620 --> 01:50:41,656
It's Dr. Meridian. Chase.

1745
01:50:43,180 --> 01:50:44,693
Do you remember me?

1746
01:50:46,580 --> 01:50:48,855
EDWARD: [Whispers] How could I forget?

1747
01:50:49,940 --> 01:50:51,771
Dr. Burton tells me...

1748
01:50:52,900 --> 01:50:54,731
...you know who Batman is.

1749
01:50:55,700 --> 01:50:58,578
EDWARD: I can't tell you
if you don't say, "please."

1750
01:50:59,940 --> 01:51:01,453
Edward, please.

1751
01:51:01,660 --> 01:51:03,139
Who is Batman?

1752
01:51:05,780 --> 01:51:06,929
I'm...

1753
01:51:07,300 --> 01:51:08,619
...Batman.

1754
01:51:08,700 --> 01:51:10,497
[Cackles hysterically]

1755
01:51:33,860 --> 01:51:35,612
Your secret is safe.

1756
01:51:35,780 --> 01:51:37,771
He is definitely a wacko.

1757
01:51:38,980 --> 01:51:40,049
"Wacko?"

1758
01:51:40,260 --> 01:51:41,932
Is that a technical term?

1759
01:51:42,580 --> 01:51:43,899
BRUCE: Listen...

1760
01:51:47,060 --> 01:51:49,130
...I won't need this anymore.

1761
01:51:52,500 --> 01:51:55,014
Thank you for giving me a new dream.

1762
01:52:11,220 --> 01:52:12,812
Don't work too late.

1763
01:52:22,060 --> 01:52:24,130
<i>[Batman Forever theme song plays]</i>

1764
01:52:41,180 --> 01:52:43,250
Subtitles conformed by SOFTITLER
